#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""wake: loom's clock piece (loom-clock). An agent's self-set alarms and schedules (relays moved to loom's runtime).

Every wake session can end by setting the next alarm; recurrence is a chain
of self-set wakes, or a schedule. If the spool ever empties, a dead-man wake
fires in ~24h so the agent always at least gets to decide.

  wake at "2026-08-05 03:13" -f routines/triage.md --note "triage"
  wake at "03:13" -p "inline prompt" --note "what it's for"   # next occurrence of 03:13
  wake in 4h -p "check the soak" --note "task 12, round 2"
  wake park --on q-1a2b3c4d -p "what to do next" --note "task 12 round 2"   # blocked on the owner: wake on the answer, then end
  wake list
  wake log [--since 24h] [--grep fire]   # the clock's own record (wake.log), newest last
  wake cancel w-abc123
  wake pause | wake resume   # hold every wake (each fires once, in order, on resume)
  wake now [--note …]        # a wake in a minute with no lane: look at what deserves attention
  wake rearm        # after boot: recreate transient timers from the spool
  wake run          # (service) rearm every clock, then keep every pending wake's timer armed
  wake reap         # (service) stop a session it started that waits on a permission prompt (WAKE_STUCK_AFTER)
  wake fire w-abc123  # (internal: invoked by the systemd transient timer)
  wake schedule set nightly --at 22:44 -f routines/nightly.md --note "…"   # a recurring wake
  wake schedule set weekly --at 17:47 --days sun -f routines/weekly.md     #   (edit = set again)
  wake schedule list | wake schedule rm <name>
  wake --agent bo …   # another agent's clock (the owner; an agent's own token picks its own)
  wake api --json     # loom's clock piece (POST /api/clock/run): a house sets its wakes here

Every agent has its own clock: its own spool under $WAKE_DATA/<agent>, at most
50 pending one-off wakes, and schedules: a recurring wake keeps exactly one
occurrence pending and arms the next when it fires, so a lane needn't re-arm
itself (a lane that still tries is told it's already scheduled). Through loom's
piece API an agent manages its own clock, all of it; the owner sees and manages
every agent's.

One agent is this machine's own (WAKE_LOCAL_AGENT): its lane files are in
WAKE_REPO, and its wakes may run here. Fire mode: "local" (default) runs them
here (loom's runtime runs their bodies: WAKE_LOCAL_RUN, below);
"house" asks loom-box for a house on the agent's primary with the wake as its
task; "mixed" sends only the wakes whose prompt says it's ready (a line
`<!-- house: ready -->` in a lane file's first 30 lines, or anywhere in an
inline prompt) and runs the rest here. Every other agent's wake, and an agent's
own wake (set through the piece API), always goes to a house. Set by $WAKE_FIRE,
else $WAKE_DATA/fire (one word).

Delivery (WAKE_DELIVERY): a wake bound for the agent's house is delivered
through loom's `POST /api/loom/deliver` (loom docs/specs/agent-runtime.md,
"Delivery") with the clock's own piece token (WAKE_DELIVER_TOKEN_FILE): the
runtime records the wake in the agent's conversation and reaches its body.
One lane is one conversation (place `lane:<name>`); any other wake is its own
(`wake:<id>`). "spawn" keeps the old path (`loom box up` with the wake as the
house's task); unset, it's "deliver" when the clock has a token for it and
loom has a piece offering delivery, else "spawn". A wake with a house slot
still goes the old way: delivery keeps no slot.

A wake that runs here (fire mode "local") is delivered too (t-1921), with the
contract's `local: true` (its `<!-- house: local -->` line taken out: the
field says it, never the words): the runtime runs its body on loom's machine,
so model choice, fallback, permissions and the stuck-session stop live in one
place. Its conversation is the one it names (`--place alert:host-watch`, set on
loom's machine only), else `local-lane:<name>` for a lane (a lane's house runs
are `lane:<name>`, and a conversation's bodies run in one place only), else
`wake:<id>`. If the runtime won't run it here (400 or 403: no local bodies for
this agent), it's a session here (WAKE_SESSION_COMMAND), said once a day.
WAKE_LOCAL_RUN=session is the way back: every local wake a session here again,
as before t-1921, except one that names its place. The clock's own stuck-session
stop (`wake reap`) still watches every session it starts; the runtime stops its
own bodies (LOOM_RUNTIME_STUCK_AFTER).

Timers: transient `systemd-run --user` units named wake-<id> (KillMode=process
so a background session the wake started survives the service's cgroup cleanup).

Settings (environment; a managed piece gets them from loom, see README.md):
  WAKE_DATA, WAKE_LOCAL_AGENT, WAKE_REPO, WAKE_LANE_DIRS, WAKE_AGENTS, WAKE_FIRE,
  WAKE_MODEL, WAKE_SESSION_COMMAND, WAKE_STUCK_AFTER, WAKE_TASK_COMMENT, WAKE_ALERT_COMMAND, WAKE_FIRE_GATE,
  WAKE_PREAMBLE_FILE, WAKE_HOUSEHOLD, WAKE_LOOM, WAKE_APPROVALS, WAKE_PRINCIPAL,
  WAKE_DELIVERY, WAKE_DELIVER_TOKEN_FILE, WAKE_LOOM_URL, WAKE_LOCAL_RUN

On whose behalf (t-1943): every wake and schedule records `for`, whom it is for. Set on loom's machine, the owner's;
set over the piece API, what the body's principal statement says once loom's runtime verifies it (`WAKE_PRINCIPAL
--verify`, default `loom runtime principal`) and it names the calling agent: "owner", a person's slug, else "-"
(unknown). The house wrapper appends `--principal <statement>` to every clock call; the API door takes it off. Just
before a delivery the clock hands the wake's `for` to the runtime (`--wake --agent … --place … --for …`), so a wake
can't turn someone else's request into the owner's.
"""

import argparse
import fcntl
import json
import hashlib
import os
import re
import secrets
import shlex
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import time
import unicodedata
import urllib.error
import urllib.request
from datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone
from pathlib import Path

HOME = Path.home()
SELF = Path(__file__).resolve()


def foreign_piece():
    """True when loom's piece variables are another piece's: the tasks piece runs `loom-clock in 1m …` when the
    owner comments, loom's runtime runs it for an alert, and both hand on their own LOOM_PIECE_NAME and
    LOOM_PIECE_HOME. Read as the clock's, those made a second clock in that piece's data, with none of the
    owner's settings: an agent called "agent", the default session command, a dead-man wake a day (t-1854)."""
    name = os.environ.get("LOOM_PIECE_NAME")
    return bool(name) and name != "clock"


def piece_home():
    """This piece's home under loom (`$LOOM_HOME/pieces/clock`): loom says so when it runs us
    (LOOM_PIECE_HOME); run directly (a timer, a body typing `wake`), it's found from where this
    file lives, so every way in reads the same clocks."""
    h = os.environ.get("LOOM_PIECE_HOME")
    if h and not foreign_piece():
        return Path(h)
    for d in [SELF.parent, *SELF.parents][:8]:
        if (d / "piece.json").is_file() and (d / "versions").is_dir():
            return d
    return None


PIECE_HOME = piece_home()


def _owner_settings():
    try:
        d = json.loads((PIECE_HOME / "settings.json").read_text()) if PIECE_HOME else {}
        return d if isinstance(d, dict) else {}
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return {}


_SETTINGS = _owner_settings()


def setting(name, default=""):
    """A setting: the environment (loom puts the owner's settings there), else the owner's
    settings.json in the piece home (a direct run), else the default."""
    v = os.environ.get(name)
    if v in (None, ""):
        v = _SETTINGS.get(name)
    return v if isinstance(v, str) and v != "" else default


def argv_setting(name, default):
    """A command setting: a JSON list of strings, or a plain command line (split like a shell)."""
    raw = setting(name)
    if not raw:
        return list(default)
    try:
        v = json.loads(raw) if raw.lstrip().startswith("[") else shlex.split(raw)
    except ValueError:
        sys.exit(f"wake: {name} is a JSON list of strings or a command line, not {raw!r}")
    if not isinstance(v, list) or not all(isinstance(a, str) for a in v):
        sys.exit(f"wake: {name} is a JSON list of strings or a command line")
    return v


AGENT_NAME = re.compile(r"^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,39}$")
LOCAL_AGENT = setting("WAKE_LOCAL_AGENT", "agent")
if not AGENT_NAME.match(LOCAL_AGENT):
    sys.exit(f"wake: WAKE_LOCAL_AGENT is an agent's id (lowercase letters, digits and dashes), not {LOCAL_AGENT!r}")
AGENT = LOCAL_AGENT
# The local agent's repo: its lane files, and the working directory its sessions start in.
REPO = Path(setting("WAKE_REPO") or HOME).expanduser()
LANE_DIRS = [d.strip().strip("/") for d in setting("WAKE_LANE_DIRS", "routines,briefs").split(",") if d.strip()]
# Every agent's clock is a directory under CLOCKS; the household's lanes sit beside them.
CLOCKS = Path(setting("WAKE_DATA") or (PIECE_HOME / "data" if PIECE_HOME else HOME / ".local" / "state" / "loom-clock")).expanduser()
WAKE_DIR = CLOCKS / AGENT
SPOOL = WAKE_DIR / "spool.jsonl"
LOCK = WAKE_DIR / "spool.lock"
LOG = WAKE_DIR / "wake.log"
SCHEDULES = WAKE_DIR / "schedules.json"
PAUSED = WAKE_DIR / "paused"
HOUSEHOLD = Path(setting("WAKE_HOUSEHOLD") or Path(os.environ.get("LOOM_HOME") or HOME / ".config" / "loom") / "household.json").expanduser()
# Loom lanes: household work on a schedule, assigned to an agent. The lane's text, schedule and
# assignee are the household's (here, and in the bundle); it runs as a schedule in the assignee's clock.
LANES = CLOCKS / "lanes.json"
LANE_INLINE_MAX = 6500
# A body blocked on the owner's answer parks instead of polling: the clock checks the request
# every PARK_CHECK, with no body, and wakes the continuation when the owner answers (or at PARK_FOR).
PARK_CHECK = timedelta(minutes=5)
PARK_FOR = timedelta(hours=24)
PARK_ON = re.compile(r"^(q|a)-[0-9a-f]{8}$")
MAX_PENDING = 50
SCHEDULE_NAME = re.compile(r"^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,39}$")
SLOT_NAME = re.compile(r"^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,39}$")
DAYS = ["mon", "tue", "wed", "thu", "fri", "sat", "sun"]


def configure(agent):
    """Point this run at one agent's clock."""
    global AGENT, WAKE_DIR, SPOOL, LOCK, LOG, SCHEDULES, PAUSED
    if not AGENT_NAME.match(agent or ""):
        sys.exit(f"wake: no agent {agent!r}")
    AGENT = agent
    WAKE_DIR = CLOCKS / agent
    SPOOL, LOCK, LOG = WAKE_DIR / "spool.jsonl", WAKE_DIR / "spool.lock", WAKE_DIR / "wake.log"
    SCHEDULES, PAUSED = WAKE_DIR / "schedules.json", WAKE_DIR / "paused"


def clock_agents():
    """Every agent that has a clock here (the local agent's always)."""
    out = [LOCAL_AGENT]
    if CLOCKS.is_dir():
        out += sorted(d.name for d in CLOCKS.iterdir() if d.is_dir() and AGENT_NAME.match(d.name) and d.name != LOCAL_AGENT)
    return out


DEFAULT_MODEL = setting("WAKE_MODEL", "claude-sonnet-5")
DEADMAN_HOURS = 24
LOOM = setting("WAKE_LOOM", "loom")
FIRE_CONF = CLOCKS / "fire"
# A remote caller's -f must name a lane file in the repo, never a path on
# loom's machine at large: what -f names becomes a house's task.
PROMPT_ROOTS = tuple(REPO / d for d in LANE_DIRS)
REMOTE_VERBS = {"at", "in", "park", "list", "cancel", "log", "schedule", "relay", "relays", "lane"}
TIME_FMT = "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S"
# The environment a timer's `wake fire` needs to find this clock and its tools again: the
# transient unit starts from the user manager's environment, not ours.
TIMER_ENV = ("PATH", "HOME", "LOOM_HOME", "LOOM_PIECE_NAME", "LOOM_PIECE_HOME", "LOOM_URL", "LOOM_TOKEN_FILE",
             "WAKE_DATA", "WAKE_LOCAL_AGENT", "WAKE_REPO", "WAKE_LANE_DIRS", "WAKE_AGENTS", "WAKE_FIRE", "WAKE_MODEL",
             "WAKE_SESSION_COMMAND", "WAKE_STUCK_AFTER", "WAKE_TASK_COMMENT", "WAKE_ALERT_COMMAND", "WAKE_FIRE_GATE", "WAKE_PREAMBLE_FILE",
             "WAKE_HOUSEHOLD", "WAKE_LOOM", "WAKE_APPROVALS", "WAKE_PRINCIPAL",
             "WAKE_DELIVERY", "WAKE_DELIVER_TOKEN_FILE", "WAKE_LOOM_URL", "WAKE_LOCAL_RUN")


def lane_dir():
    """Where the page's lane picker looks: the first of WAKE_LANE_DIRS."""
    return LANE_DIRS[0] if LANE_DIRS else "routines"


def repo_relative(path):
    """A lane file as the page says it: relative to the repo when it's in it."""
    p = str(path or "")
    return Path(p).relative_to(REPO).as_posix() if p.startswith(str(REPO).rstrip("/") + "/") else p


def lane_dirs_text():
    return " or ".join(f"{d}/" for d in LANE_DIRS) or "routines/"


def approvals_argv():
    """The approvals piece, as loom reaches it (`loom approvals`), unless WAKE_APPROVALS names it."""
    return argv_setting("WAKE_APPROVALS", [LOOM, "approvals"])


# ─── On whose behalf (t-1943) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# The owner's standing permissions (his merge rules, say) cover work a body does for him; work it does for someone
# else (a person who messaged it in Slack or Discord) needs that person's own grant, or it asks. Who a body acts for is
# its principal, and loom's runtime is the root of trust for it. A wake keeps the principal of the body that set it, so
# a wake can't turn a non-owner's request into the owner's: `for` on every wake and schedule is "owner", a person's
# slug, or "-" (unknown, which the runtime treats as not the owner).
PRINCIPAL_SLUG = re.compile(r"^[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*$")
PRINCIPAL_TIMEOUT_S = 5


def principal_argv():
    """The runtime's principal command (`loom runtime principal`), unless WAKE_PRINCIPAL names it."""
    return argv_setting("WAKE_PRINCIPAL", [LOOM, "runtime", "principal"])


def split_principal(argv):
    """argv without the `--principal <statement>` the house wrapper appends to every clock call from a body that has
    one, and that statement ("" when there's none). Only trailing pairs: the wrapper appends, so one in the middle is a
    body's own words, and argparse refuses it. With more than one, the last is the wrapper's, even an empty one (which
    is none: an earlier one is never used in its place)."""
    argv, statement, found = list(argv), "", False
    while True:
        if len(argv) >= 2 and argv[-2] == "--principal":
            statement, argv = (statement if found else argv[-1]), argv[:-2]
        elif argv and argv[-1].startswith("--principal="):
            statement, argv = (statement if found else argv[-1].split("=", 1)[1]), argv[:-1]
        else:
            return argv, statement
        found = True


def caller_agent():
    """The agent the piece API says is calling: its origin (`agent:<name>`), else WAKE_CALLER's agent."""
    origin = os.environ.get("WAKE_ORIGIN", "").strip()
    if origin.startswith("agent:"):
        return origin.split(":", 1)[1]
    try:
        caller = json.loads(os.environ.get("WAKE_CALLER") or "{}")
    except ValueError:
        return None
    return caller.get("agent") if isinstance(caller, dict) and caller.get("kind") == "agent" else None


def verify_principal(statement):
    """The runtime's reading of a principal statement (`<cmd> --verify`, the statement on stdin): its verified fields,
    or None when it's invalid or can't be read. The statement itself is never logged or printed: only these fields."""
    try:
        r = subprocess.run([*principal_argv(), "--verify"], input=statement, capture_output=True, text=True,
                           timeout=PRINCIPAL_TIMEOUT_S, env={k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if k != "HOUSE_ID"})
        v = json.loads(r.stdout) if r.returncode == 0 else None
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError, ValueError, SystemExit) as e:  # SystemExit: WAKE_PRINCIPAL malformed
        log("principal-fail", f"the runtime's principal command didn't verify ({type(e).__name__}): taken as unknown")
        return None
    return v if isinstance(v, dict) and v.get("ok") is True else None


_PRINCIPAL = {}


def principal_for():
    """Whom a wake or schedule set by this run is for. On loom's machine (no WAKE_ORIGIN, the owner's own account and
    the household's lanes): the owner. Over the piece API: what the caller's verified statement says, when it is this
    same agent's ("owner", or the person's slug); no statement, one that doesn't verify, or one for another agent: "-"."""
    if not os.environ.get("WAKE_ORIGIN", "").strip():
        return "owner"
    statement = os.environ.get("WAKE_PRINCIPAL_STATEMENT", "")
    agent = caller_agent()
    # Once per run: the wake, its approval and that approval's spend all say the same.
    key = (statement, agent)
    if key not in _PRINCIPAL:
        v = verify_principal(statement) if statement else None
        if not v or not agent or v.get("agent") != agent:
            _PRINCIPAL[key] = "-"
        elif v.get("owner") is True:
            _PRINCIPAL[key] = "owner"
        else:
            f = v.get("for")
            # A person whose slug is "owner" is a person, not the owner: unknown here (the words are the same).
            _PRINCIPAL[key] = f if isinstance(f, str) and PRINCIPAL_SLUG.match(f) and f != "owner" else "-"
    return _PRINCIPAL[key]


def narrower(a, b):
    """The narrower of two principals: the owner's is the widest, and two different people make it unknown."""
    if a == b or b == "owner":
        return a
    return b if a == "owner" else "-"


def entry_for(entry):
    """A wake's principal; one set before t-1943 has none: the owner's when it was set on loom's machine, else unknown."""
    v = entry.get("for")
    if v is None:
        return "-" if entry.get("origin") else "owner"
    return v if v in ("owner", "-") or (isinstance(v, str) and PRINCIPAL_SLUG.match(v)) else "-"


def hand_over_principal(agent, place, delivery_id, for_):
    """Tell the runtime whom the wake about to be delivered is for (`<cmd> --wake --agent … --place … --id … --for …`),
    for exactly that delivery (its id). Not fatal: a failure is logged, the delivery goes ahead, and the runtime treats
    the wake as unknown (it fails closed)."""
    try:
        r = subprocess.run([*principal_argv(), "--wake", "--agent", agent, "--place", place, "--id", delivery_id, "--for", for_],
                           capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=PRINCIPAL_TIMEOUT_S, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL,
                           env={k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if k != "HOUSE_ID"})
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError, SystemExit) as e:  # SystemExit: WAKE_PRINCIPAL malformed
        log("principal-fail", f"{place} for={for_}: the runtime's principal command didn't run ({e}); delivered as unknown")
        return False
    if r.returncode != 0:
        log("principal-fail", f"{place} for={for_}: exit {r.returncode} {(r.stderr or '').strip()[:200]}; delivered as unknown")
        return False
    return True


PREAMBLE = """You are {name}, waking from a self-set alarm {where} \
(wake id {id}, kind {kind}, set {created}{note}). This session was dispatched \
by loom's clock piece (`wake`). Load identity first, then do the work \
below. Before you end: reflect, and set your next wake(s) with the `wake` CLI \
(`wake in 4h -p ... --note ...`, `wake at "03:13" -f {lanes}/x.md`, `wake list`); a -p \
wake runs in a fresh house, so put `<!-- house: local -->` in its prompt only \
if it needs loom's machine itself. If a recurring duty brought you here and it \
has no schedule, re-arm it yourself: recurrence is a chain of self-set wakes. If \
you set nothing, a dead-man wake fires in ~24h. Before you end (and at the start \
of anything long) leave your own episode in loom (mcp__loom__remember, category \
"episode", metadata {{"where": "wake:{id}"}}).

---

{body}"""


def preamble_template():
    """The words every wake's session starts with: WAKE_PREAMBLE_FILE if the instance has its own
    (the same {name} {where} {id} {kind} {created} {note} {lanes} {body} fields), else the piece's."""
    f = setting("WAKE_PREAMBLE_FILE")
    if f:
        try:
            return Path(f).expanduser().read_text()
        except OSError:
            log("preamble", f"WAKE_PREAMBLE_FILE {f} can't be read; the piece's own is used")
    return PREAMBLE


NOW_PROMPT = """Woken now: {who} asked for a wake from loom's Clock page, \
with no lane. Look at what deserves attention: your work queue, recent loom \
memory, Your call, the state of the machine. Do something useful or file what you \
find."""

DEADMAN_PROMPT = """Dead-man wake: the spool was empty, so this default alarm \
fired. Nothing was scheduled: decide what deserves attention. Review your \
work queue, recent loom memory, and the state of the machine. Do something \
useful or file what you find, and do not end without setting at least one \
real wake."""


def log(event, detail=""):
    WAKE_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    with open(LOG, "a") as f:
        f.write(f"{datetime.now().strftime(TIME_FMT)} | {event} | {detail}\n")


class Spool:
    """Locked read-modify-write access to the wake spool."""

    def __enter__(self):
        WAKE_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        self._lock = open(LOCK, "w")
        fcntl.flock(self._lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        self.entries = []
        if SPOOL.exists():
            for line in SPOOL.read_text().splitlines():
                if line.strip():
                    self.entries.append(json.loads(line))
        return self

    def __exit__(self, *exc):
        # Write self.entries regardless of exc: by the time a caller raises
        # partway through a block (arm_timer's sys.exit on a systemd-run
        # failure, say), any irreversible side effect it already ran
        # (disarm_timer, an earlier arm_timer) is already reflected there.
        # Discarding the write on exception reverts the spool to a stale
        # state that no longer matches those side effects instead of
        # recording what actually happened: a retry that was armed and
        # then vanished from the spool.
        tmp = SPOOL.with_suffix(".tmp")
        tmp.write_text("".join(json.dumps(e) + "\n" for e in self.entries))
        tmp.replace(SPOOL)
        fcntl.flock(self._lock, fcntl.LOCK_UN)
        self._lock.close()
        return False


def parse_at(tokens):
    """Accept 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM[:SS]', 'HH:MM' (next occurrence), 'tomorrow HH:MM'."""
    s = " ".join(tokens)
    now = datetime.now()
    for fmt in ("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S", "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M"):
        try:
            return datetime.strptime(s, fmt)
        except ValueError:
            pass
    m = re.fullmatch(r"(tomorrow )?(\d{1,2}):(\d{2})", s)
    if m:
        t = now.replace(hour=int(m[2]), minute=int(m[3]), second=0, microsecond=0)
        if m[1] or t <= now:
            t += timedelta(days=1)
        return t
    sys.exit(f"wake: can't parse time {s!r}")


def parse_in(tokens):
    s = "".join(tokens)
    parts = re.findall(r"(\d+)([smhd])", s)
    if not parts or "".join(n + u for n, u in parts) != s:
        sys.exit(f"wake: can't parse duration {s!r} (want e.g. 90m, 4h, 1h30m, 2d)")
    secs = sum(int(n) * {"s": 1, "m": 60, "h": 3600, "d": 86400}[u] for n, u in parts)
    return datetime.now() + timedelta(seconds=secs)


def unit_name(wid):
    return f"wake-{wid}"


def unit_loaded(wid):
    """True if wake-<wid>'s timer unit is already loaded.

    Checked via systemctl's LoadState, not systemd-run's stderr wording:
    on systemd 257 a unit-name collision fails with "Unit <name> was
    already loaded or has a fragment file." -- never the older "already
    exists" text an earlier check looked for.
    """
    r = subprocess.run(
        ["systemctl", "--user", "show", "-p", "LoadState", "--value",
         unit_name(wid) + ".timer"],
        capture_output=True, text=True)
    return r.returncode == 0 and r.stdout.strip() == "loaded"


def stable_self():
    """The path a timer runs: loom's link to this piece (`$LOOM_HOME/pieces/bin/loom-clock`) when it's a
    managed piece, which outlives an update; this file's own path otherwise. A timer armed with a
    version's own path would break once that version is deleted."""
    if PIECE_HOME:
        link = PIECE_HOME.parent / "bin" / "loom-clock"
        if link.exists():
            return link
    return SELF


def timer_env():
    """--setenv for a timer: what this run was configured with, so the fired run reads the same clocks."""
    out = []
    for k in TIMER_ENV:
        v = os.environ.get(k)
        if k in ("LOOM_PIECE_NAME", "LOOM_PIECE_HOME", "LOOM_TOKEN_FILE") and foreign_piece():
            v = str(PIECE_HOME) if k == "LOOM_PIECE_HOME" and PIECE_HOME else None
        if v not in (None, "") and "\n" not in v:
            out += ["--setenv", f"{k}={v}"]
    return out


def arm_timer(entry):
    """Create the transient timer for a spool entry. Past-due → ~1min out."""
    at = datetime.strptime(entry["at"], TIME_FMT)
    if at <= datetime.now():
        at = datetime.now() + timedelta(seconds=60)
    r = subprocess.run(
        ["systemd-run", "--user", "--collect",
         "--unit", unit_name(entry["id"]),
         "--on-calendar", at.strftime(TIME_FMT),
         "--timer-property", "AccuracySec=30s",
         "--property", "KillMode=process",
         "--property", f"WorkingDirectory={REPO if REPO.is_dir() else HOME}",
         *timer_env(),
         str(stable_self()), "--agent", AGENT, "fire", entry["id"]],
        capture_output=True, text=True)
    if r.returncode != 0:
        if unit_loaded(entry["id"]):
            return "exists"
        sys.exit(f"wake: systemd-run failed: {r.stderr.strip()}")
    return "armed"


def disarm_timer(wid):
    for suffix in (".timer", ".service"):
        subprocess.run(["systemctl", "--user", "stop", unit_name(wid) + suffix],
                       capture_output=True)


def ensure_deadman(spool):
    """Empty spool → plant the dead-man wake so there is always a next wake."""
    if spool.entries:
        return
    entry = {
        "id": "w-" + secrets.token_hex(3),
        "kind": "deadman",
        "at": (datetime.now() + timedelta(hours=DEADMAN_HOURS)).strftime(TIME_FMT),
        "note": "dead-man default: spool emptied",
        "prompt": DEADMAN_PROMPT,
        "model": DEFAULT_MODEL,
        "for": "owner",  # the clock's own default, with its own fixed words: nobody's request
        "created": datetime.now().strftime(TIME_FMT),
    }
    spool.entries.append(entry)
    arm_timer(entry)
    log("deadman", f"{entry['id']} at {entry['at']}")


def looks_like_path(prompt):
    """True when `prompt` is shaped like a file path, not prose.

    Catches the -p/-f mixup (`-p routines/x.md` dispatches the literal string,
    not the file): a bare, space-free token that has a slash, ends in .md, or
    names a file that actually exists in the repo or one of its lane
    directories. A real inline prompt has spaces; this never flags one.
    """
    s = prompt.strip()
    if not s or re.search(r"\s", s):
        return False
    if "/" in s or s.endswith(".md"):
        return True
    for base in (REPO, *PROMPT_ROOTS):
        try:
            if (base / s).is_file():
                return True
        except OSError:
            pass
    return False


def load_schedules():
    try:
        return json.loads(SCHEDULES.read_text())
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return {}


def save_schedules(scheds):
    WAKE_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    tmp = SCHEDULES.with_suffix(".tmp")
    tmp.write_text(json.dumps(scheds, indent=1, sort_keys=True))
    tmp.replace(SCHEDULES)


def days_of(spec):
    """'mon-fri', 'sat,sun', 'sun' -> weekday numbers (all seven when empty)."""
    if not spec:
        return set(range(7))
    out = set()
    for part in spec.lower().split(","):
        if "-" in part:
            a, b = part.split("-", 1)
            i, j = DAYS.index(a), DAYS.index(b)
            out |= set(range(i, j + 1)) if i <= j else set(range(i, 7)) | set(range(0, j + 1))
        else:
            out.add(DAYS.index(part))
    return out


def next_occurrence(sched, after):
    """The first of a schedule's times strictly after `after` (local, naive)."""
    days = days_of(sched.get("days"))
    times = [sched["at"]] if isinstance(sched["at"], str) else sched["at"]
    best = None
    for t in times:
        h, m = map(int, t.split(":"))
        d = after.replace(hour=h, minute=m, second=0, microsecond=0)
        if d <= after:
            d += timedelta(days=1)
        while d.weekday() not in days:
            d += timedelta(days=1)
        best = d if best is None or d < best else best
    return best


def schedule_entry(name, sched, at):
    entry = {
        "id": "w-" + secrets.token_hex(3),
        "kind": "schedule",
        "schedule": name,
        "at": at.strftime(TIME_FMT),
        "note": f"schedule {name}" + (f": {sched['note']}" if sched.get("note") else ""),
        "model": sched.get("model") or DEFAULT_MODEL,
        "created": datetime.now().strftime(TIME_FMT),
    }
    # Its principal goes with it, like its origin: an occurrence is for whomever the schedule was set for.
    for k in ("prompt", "prompt_file", "lane", "origin", "for", "slot"):
        if sched.get(k):
            entry[k] = sched[k]
    return entry


def schedule_for_file(path):
    """The schedule that already runs this lane file, if any."""
    for name, sc in load_schedules().items():
        # A loom lane set from a file counts too: its run's own "re-arm yourself" is answered, not doubled.
        for f in (sc.get("prompt_file"), sc.get("lane_file")):
            if f and Path(f).resolve() == Path(path).resolve():
                return name
    return None


def cmd_set(args, when):
    if getattr(args, "approval", ""):
        # A local wake the owner allowed is set with the words this clock filed for it, byte for byte, and only those:
        # a continuation in a later house can't be trusted to retype them, and a body that brings its own words could
        # bring other words with the same short hash. Other words, or an id this clock filed no wake for, are refused
        # before anything is spent.
        if args.prompt_file:
            sys.exit("wake: --approval is for a local wake the clock asked the owner about, not a lane file (-f)")
        filed = filed_wakes().get(args.approval)
        if not filed:
            sys.exit(f"wake: this clock filed no local wake as {args.approval}. Set the wake again with its words (-p, "
                     "no --approval): the clock asks the owner and keeps those words for the continuation")
        if args.prompt and args.prompt != filed["prompt"]:
            sys.exit(f"wake: {args.approval} was allowed for other words than these. Set it without -p "
                     f"(wake in 1m --approval {args.approval}): the clock uses exactly the words the owner allowed")
        # The note too: it's read into the session's opening words, so it's part of what runs, and the owner's card
        # showed the note it was filed with. A different one is refused, before anything is spent.
        if args.note and args.note != filed["note"]:
            sys.exit(f"wake: {args.approval} was filed with its own note; set it without --note (or with exactly that "
                     "one): a note is part of what the session reads, and the owner allowed that one")
        args.prompt = filed["prompt"]
        args.note = filed["note"]
        # The spool's limit before the spend: a refusal after it would use up the owner's yes for nothing.
        with Spool() as spool:
            if sum(1 for e in spool.entries if e["kind"] in ("wake", "parked")) >= MAX_PENDING:
                sys.exit(f"wake: {AGENT} has {MAX_PENDING} one-off wakes pending already; cancel some first (wake list)")
        if filed.get("target") != f"{AGENT}:{hashlib.sha256(args.prompt.encode()).hexdigest()[:16]}":
            sys.exit(f"wake: the words this clock kept for {args.approval} don't match what it filed; set the wake again with -p")
    if bool(args.prompt) == bool(args.prompt_file):
        sys.exit("wake: exactly one of --prompt/-p or --prompt-file/-f required")
    if args.prompt and looks_like_path(args.prompt):
        sys.exit(
            f"wake: --prompt/-p looks like a file path ({args.prompt!r}) — "
            "did you mean --prompt-file/-f? (-p sends its words as the prompt, "
            "so -p routines/x.md would dispatch the literal string, not the file's content)"
        )
    if args.prompt and not args.note.strip():
        sys.exit(
            "wake: -p/--prompt wakes require --note saying what the wake is for "
            "(the task and round, say): the note is what makes a wake legible in "
            "`wake list`, the log and loom's page without reading its whole prompt"
        )
    entry = {
        "id": "w-" + secrets.token_hex(3),
        "kind": "wake",
        "at": when.strftime(TIME_FMT),
        "note": args.note or "",
        "model": args.model,
        "created": datetime.now().strftime(TIME_FMT),
    }
    origin = os.environ.get("WAKE_ORIGIN", "").strip()
    if origin:
        entry["origin"] = origin
    # On whose behalf: the owner's on loom's machine, else what the body's verified principal says (or unknown).
    entry["for"] = principal_for()
    place = (getattr(args, "place", "") or "").strip()
    if place:
        # A place is a conversation: what's delivered there feeds the body that has it. Set here, on loom's machine,
        # only: a house naming a place could feed its words to a body that runs on loom's machine.
        if origin:
            sys.exit("wake: --place is for wakes set on loom's machine; a house's wake is its own conversation")
        if not PLACE.fullmatch(place) or place.startswith(("lane:", "wake:")):
            sys.exit(f"wake: --place is <kind>:<name> (like alert:host-watch), not lane:/wake: (the clock's own), not {place!r}")
        if args.slot:
            sys.exit("wake: --place and --slot don't go together: a delivered wake keeps a conversation, not a slot")
        entry["place"] = place
    if args.slot:
        if not SLOT_NAME.match(args.slot):
            sys.exit(f"wake: --slot is lowercase letters, digits and dashes, not {args.slot!r}")
        entry["slot"] = args.slot
    if args.prompt:
        entry["prompt"] = args.prompt
        # A house's wake runs in a house: a steered body mustn't put itself on loom's machine. One
        # that says it needs loom's machine is told so at once (rather than silently sent to a
        # house), and runs there only with the owner's approval, for exactly this prompt.
        # With --approval the approval is spent here too (on loom's machine as well), so one Allow runs it once.
        if (origin or getattr(args, "approval", "")) and HOUSE_LOCAL in args.prompt:
            target = f"{AGENT}:{hashlib.sha256(args.prompt.encode()).hexdigest()[:16]}"
            if not getattr(args, "approval", ""):
                # The clock files the ask itself, with the prompt as its words: the owner approves what
                # will run, not the body's own description of it.
                body = args.prompt.replace(HOUSE_LOCAL, "").strip()
                # All of it on the card, or no ask: a long prompt could look harmless in its first
                # lines and do something else after them.
                if len(body) > LOCAL_WAKE_MAX:
                    sys.exit(f"wake: a local wake's prompt is {LOCAL_WAKE_MAX} characters at most, so the owner's card shows "
                             "all of it; say plainly what it does on loom's machine")
                aid = file_approval("local-wake", target, f"run on loom's machine: {body}", f"set from a house, note: {args.note}")
                remember_filed(aid, target, args.prompt, args.note)
                sys.exit("wake: a wake set from a house runs in a house; <!-- house: local --> needs the owner's approval. "
                         + f"Asked them ({aid}, a card on loom's Home with this prompt). Park on it "
                           f"(wake park --on {aid} -p \"<what to do next>\" --note …) and end: once it's allowed, the "
                           f"continuation sets it with `wake in 1m --approval {aid}`, no -p, and the clock uses these exact words."
                         + " Most work needs no host: a house can do it.")
            no = spend_approval(args.approval, "local-wake", target)
            if no:
                sys.exit(f"wake: approval {args.approval} isn't allowed for this local wake: {no}")
            entry["local_approval"] = args.approval
    elif AGENT != LOCAL_AGENT:
        # Another agent's lane files are in its own repo, not here: the house reads it.
        if not re.fullmatch(r"[A-Za-z0-9._/-]{1,200}\.md", args.prompt_file) or ".." in args.prompt_file.split("/"):
            sys.exit(f"wake: a lane file is a path in your repo, like routines/x.md, not {args.prompt_file}")
        entry["lane"] = args.prompt_file
    else:
        pf = Path(args.prompt_file)
        if not pf.is_absolute():
            pf = REPO / pf
        if origin and lane_file(pf) is None:
            sys.exit(f"wake: a wake from {origin} takes a lane file in the repo ({lane_dirs_text()}), not {args.prompt_file}")
        if not pf.is_file():
            sys.exit(f"wake: no such prompt file: {pf}")
        # A lane that runs on a schedule needn't re-arm itself: a wake for it near
        # the schedule's next occurrence (within 6h) is that re-arm, so say so and
        # arm nothing. One further off is a real extra run.
        sched = schedule_for_file(pf)
        if sched:
            with Spool() as spool:
                nxt = [datetime.strptime(e["at"], TIME_FMT) for e in spool.entries if e.get("schedule") == sched]
            if nxt and abs(when - min(nxt)) <= timedelta(hours=6):
                print(f"already scheduled: {sched}, next at {min(nxt).strftime(TIME_FMT)} (nothing armed)")
                log("set-scheduled", f"{pf.name} is schedule {sched}; nothing armed")
                return
        entry["prompt_file"] = str(pf)
    if getattr(args, "park_on", ""):
        entry["kind"], entry["on"] = "parked", args.park_on
        # What the owner is asked to allow, as filed (kind and exact target): the continuation is handed it whole.
        card = approval_card(args.park_on) if args.park_on.startswith("a-") else None
        if card:
            entry["approval"] = card
        entry["until"] = (datetime.now() + PARK_FOR).strftime(TIME_FMT)
    with Spool() as spool:
        if sum(1 for e in spool.entries if e["kind"] in ("wake", "parked")) >= MAX_PENDING:
            sys.exit(f"wake: {AGENT} has {MAX_PENDING} one-off wakes pending already; cancel some first (wake list)")
        # A real wake replaces any pending dead-man.
        for dm in [e for e in spool.entries if e["kind"] == "deadman"]:
            disarm_timer(dm["id"])
            spool.entries.remove(dm)
            log("deadman-cleared", dm["id"])
        spool.entries.append(entry)
        arm_timer(entry)
    log("set", f"{entry['id']} at {entry['at']} note={entry['note']!r}" + (f" parked on {entry['on']}" if entry.get("on") else ""))
    if entry.get("on"):
        print(f"{entry['id']} parked on {entry['on']}: it wakes when the owner answers (checked every "
              f"{PARK_CHECK.seconds // 60} minutes; {PARK_FOR.seconds // 3600 + PARK_FOR.days * 24}h at most). End this session now.")
    else:
        print(f"{entry['id']} will wake at {entry['at']}")


def cmd_park(args):
    """Park on a request (a secret's q-…, an approval's a-…): the continuation wakes on the answer."""
    if not PARK_ON.match(args.park_on or ""):
        sys.exit("wake: park on a secret request (q-…) or an approval (a-…), by its id")
    cmd_set(args, datetime.now() + PARK_CHECK)


FILED_KEEP = timedelta(days=8)


def filed_path():
    return WAKE_DIR / "filed.json"


def filed_wakes():
    """The local wakes this clock filed approvals for, by approval id: their exact prompt, target and note."""
    try:
        d = json.loads(filed_path().read_text())
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return {}
    if not isinstance(d, dict):
        return {}
    cutoff = (datetime.now() - FILED_KEEP).strftime(TIME_FMT)
    return {k: v for k, v in d.items() if isinstance(v, dict) and isinstance(v.get("prompt"), str) and HOUSE_LOCAL in v["prompt"]
            and isinstance(v.get("note"), str) and isinstance(v.get("at"), str) and v["at"] >= cutoff}


def remember_filed(aid, target, prompt, note):
    """Keep the words a local wake's approval was filed for, so its continuation sets exactly them (cmd_set). Kept
    FILED_KEEP: longer than a park waits (PARK_FOR) and than an allowed approval lasts."""
    WAKE_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    with open(LOCK, "w") as lock:
        fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)  # the clock's lock, without rewriting the spool
        d = filed_wakes()
        d[aid] = {"target": target, "prompt": prompt, "note": note, "at": datetime.now().strftime(TIME_FMT)}
        tmp = filed_path().with_suffix(f".{os.getpid()}.tmp")
        tmp.unlink(missing_ok=True)  # a stale one keeps its old mode; O_EXCL makes a fresh 0600 file
        with os.fdopen(os.open(tmp, os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL | os.O_WRONLY, 0o600), "w") as f:
            f.write(json.dumps(d, indent=1) + "\n")
        tmp.replace(filed_path())
    log("local-wake-filed", f"{aid} target={target} note={note!r}")


def approval_card(aid):
    """The approval's kind and exact target as filed (approvals check --json, for the body this runs for), or None
    when the piece can't say: an older piece, or another agent's approval."""
    argv = [*approvals_argv(), "check", aid, "--json"]
    caller = os.environ.get("WAKE_CALLER", "").strip()
    if caller:
        argv += ["--as", caller]
    try:
        # Short: over the piece API the whole wake call has 12 seconds, and a park without the card still parks.
        r = subprocess.run(argv, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=5,
                           env={k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if k != "HOUSE_ID"})
        card = json.loads(r.stdout) if r.returncode == 0 else None
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError, ValueError):
        return None
    # Only this clock's agent's own: never another agent's kind and target handed to this one's continuation.
    if not isinstance(card, dict) or card.get("id") != aid or card.get("agent") != AGENT \
            or not all(isinstance(card.get(k), str) and card[k] for k in ("kind", "target")):
        return None
    return {"kind": card["kind"], "target": card["target"]}


def spend_words(rid, card):
    """How the continuation spends the owner's yes, exactly as filed, so it never asks again in its own words."""
    filed = filed_wakes().get(rid)
    if filed:
        # Quoted for the reader without the house marker: the continuation's own prompt mustn't say it needs loom's
        # machine (house_ready reads the whole prompt), and it needn't retype the words.
        words = filed["prompt"]
        while HOUSE_LOCAL in words:  # a marker split around another comes back whole after one pass
            words = words.replace(HOUSE_LOCAL, "")
        words = words.strip()
        return (f"Pick up where you left off. It's a local wake: set it with exactly `wake in 1m --approval {rid}`, "
                f"no -p (the clock uses the words it filed for {rid}). What the owner allowed it to do: {words}")
    if (card or {}).get("kind") == "local-wake":
        # Its words are gone from this clock (expired, or filed before it kept them): nothing here can set it, and
        # spending it any other way would use up the owner's yes and run nothing.
        return (f"The clock no longer has the words {rid} was filed for, so it can't be set from it. Don't spend it: "
                f"comment on the task what was waiting, set the wake again with its words (-p) so the owner is asked "
                f"once more, and park on the new id.")
    if card:
        return (f"Pick up where you left off, and spend it on exactly the action it allows ({card['kind']} for "
                f"{card['target']}): `approvals use {rid} --kind {card['kind']} --target {shlex.quote(card['target'])}`, "
                f"or the tool that asked with this id ({rid}). Don't ask again: any of this agent's bodies spends it, once.")
    return f"Pick up where you left off, and spend it with --approval {rid} on exactly the action it allows."


def request_state(rid):
    """A request's state, read on loom's machine: secrets' q-… or approvals' a-…; 'unknown' if it can't be read."""
    argv = [LOOM, "secrets", "state", rid] if rid.startswith("q-") else [*approvals_argv(), "check", rid]
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(argv, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30,
                           env={k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if k not in ("HOUSE_ID", "WAKE_CALLER")})
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        return "unknown"
    out = r.stdout.strip()
    return out if r.returncode == 0 and re.fullmatch(r"[a-z]{3,12}", out) else "unknown"


def unpark(entry, state):
    """The parked body's continuation, told what the owner said."""
    rid = entry["on"]
    if state in ("granted", "allowed"):
        how = (f"Pick up where you left off. A secret: request it again (the secrets piece's `request <name> --why …`), "
               f"and it's granted to this house at once; then get it." if rid.startswith("q-") else
               spend_words(rid, entry.get("approval")))
        head = f"The owner allowed {rid}. {how}"
    elif state == "pending":
        head = (f"No answer to {rid} after {PARK_FOR.seconds // 3600 + PARK_FOR.days * 24}h. Leave a comment saying what's "
                f"waiting on the owner and stop; don't ask again unless the work needs it now.")
    else:
        head = (f"The owner's answer to {rid}: {state}. Don't work around it: comment on the task what's blocked and why, "
                f"and wrap up cleanly.")
    entry["kind"] = "wake"
    entry["prompt"] = f"{head}\n\n---\n\n{entry['prompt']}"
    entry["answer"] = state  # the request's id stays in entry["on"]; the note is for people
    entry["note"] = f"{resumed_words(state)}: {RESUMED.sub('', entry.get('note', ''))}"


# How a resumed wake's note starts, by the owner's answer; RESUMED strips one already there (and the older
# "unparked (a-… allowed): " form), so a note resumed twice says it once.
RESUME_WORDS = {"granted": "Resumed after your OK", "allowed": "Resumed after your OK",
                "denied": "Resumed after you said no",
                "pending": f"Resumed, no answer in {PARK_FOR.seconds // 3600 + PARK_FOR.days * 24}h",
                "expired": "Resumed, your OK expired", "unknown": "Resumed, your answer couldn't be read"}
RESUMED = re.compile(r"^(?:(?:Resumed(?: after your OK| after you said no| after your answer \([^)]*\)|, [^:]*)|unparked \([^)]*\)): )+")


def resumed_words(state):
    return RESUME_WORDS.get(state, f"Resumed after your answer ({state})")


def cmd_list(_args):
    with Spool() as spool:
        entries = sorted(spool.entries, key=lambda e: e["at"])
    if not entries:
        print("spool empty (this should not happen — dead-man missing; run: wake rearm)")
        return
    now = datetime.now()
    for e in entries:
        at = datetime.strptime(e["at"], TIME_FMT)
        delta = at - now
        mins = int(delta.total_seconds() // 60)
        rel = f"{mins // 1440}d{mins % 1440 // 60}h" if mins >= 1440 else \
              f"{mins // 60}h{mins % 60:02d}m" if mins >= 60 else f"{mins}m"
        what = e.get("note") or e.get("prompt_file") or e.get("lane") or (e.get("prompt", "")[:50])
        armed = subprocess.run(
            ["systemctl", "--user", "is-active", "--quiet", unit_name(e["id"]) + ".timer"],
            capture_output=True).returncode == 0
        flag = "" if armed else "  [NOT ARMED — run: wake rearm]"
        print(f"{e['id']}  {e['at']}  (in {rel})  [{e['kind']}]  {what}{flag}")


def cmd_log(args):
    """The clock's record, for a body that isn't on loom's machine (reflect, plan
    in a house): lines since a duration ago, optionally only those containing a word."""
    now = datetime.now()
    since = now - (parse_in([args.since]) - now)
    out = []
    try:
        lines = LOG.read_text().splitlines()
    except OSError:
        lines = []
    for line in lines:
        try:
            t = datetime.strptime(line[:19], TIME_FMT)
        except ValueError:
            continue
        if t >= since and (not args.grep or args.grep in line):
            out.append(line)
    print("\n".join(out[-2000:]))


def cmd_schedule(args):
    """Recurring wakes: set (create or replace), rm, list."""
    scheds = load_schedules()
    if args.action == "list":
        with Spool() as spool:
            nxt = {e["schedule"]: e["at"] for e in spool.entries if e.get("schedule")}
        if not scheds:
            print(f"{AGENT} has no schedules")
        for name, sc in sorted(scheds.items()):
            when = when_text(sc)
            what = sc.get("prompt_file") or sc.get("lane") or (sc.get("prompt", "")[:50])
            print(f"{name:<22} {when:<18} next {nxt.get(name, '(none armed)')}  {what}" + (f"  — {sc['note']}" if sc.get("note") else ""))
        return
    if not SCHEDULE_NAME.match(args.name or ""):
        sys.exit("wake: a schedule's name is lowercase letters, digits and dashes, like nightly")
    if args.action == "run":
        # One occurrence now, from the schedule itself: its origin, lane and
        # model come with it (an agent's own lane still goes only to a house).
        if args.name not in scheds:
            sys.exit(f"wake: {AGENT} has no schedule {args.name}")
        entry = schedule_entry(args.name, scheds[args.name], datetime.now())
        entry.update(kind="wake", note=f"{args.name} run now" + (f": {args.note}" if args.note else ""))
        del entry["schedule"]
        caller = os.environ.get("WAKE_ORIGIN", "").strip()
        if caller:
            # An agent running an owner-set schedule still only runs it in a house.
            entry["origin"] = caller
            # And for no one wider than both: a body working for someone else can't run the owner's schedule as the
            # owner's, nor the owner's body someone else's as his. On loom's machine it stays the schedule's own.
            entry["for"] = narrower(entry_for(scheds[args.name]), principal_for())
        with Spool() as spool:
            if sum(1 for e in spool.entries if e["kind"] == "wake") >= MAX_PENDING:
                sys.exit(f"wake: {AGENT} has {MAX_PENDING} one-off wakes pending already; cancel some first (wake list)")
            spool.entries.append(entry)
            arm_timer(entry)
        log("set", f"{entry['id']} at {entry['at']} note={entry['note']!r}")
        print(f"{entry['id']}: {args.name} runs within a minute")
        return
    if args.action == "rm":
        if args.name not in scheds:
            sys.exit(f"wake: {AGENT} has no schedule {args.name}")
        with Spool() as spool:
            for e in [e for e in spool.entries if e.get("schedule") == args.name]:
                disarm_timer(e["id"])
                spool.entries.remove(e)
            del scheds[args.name]
            save_schedules(scheds)
            ensure_deadman(spool)
        log("schedule-rm", args.name)
        print(f"removed schedule {args.name}")
        return
    # set
    if not args.at:
        sys.exit("wake: schedule set needs --at HH:MM (a time, or several: 07:17,19:17)")
    times = [t.strip() for t in args.at.split(",")]
    if not all(re.fullmatch(r"([01]\d|2[0-3]):[0-5]\d", t) for t in times):
        sys.exit(f"wake: --at takes HH:MM times, not {args.at!r}")
    try:
        days_of(args.days)
    except ValueError:
        sys.exit(f"wake: --days takes mon..sun, a range (mon-fri) or a list (sat,sun), not {args.days!r}")
    if bool(args.prompt) == bool(args.prompt_file):
        sys.exit("wake: a schedule runs exactly one of --prompt/-p or --prompt-file/-f")
    sc = {"at": times[0] if len(times) == 1 else times, "note": args.note or "", "model": args.model,
          "created": datetime.now().strftime(TIME_FMT)}
    if args.days:
        sc["days"] = args.days.lower()
    origin = os.environ.get("WAKE_ORIGIN", "").strip()
    if origin:
        sc["origin"] = origin
    # A loom lane is set here too, on loom's machine: the owner's. Over the API, the caller's verified principal.
    sc["for"] = principal_for()
    if args.slot:
        if not SLOT_NAME.match(args.slot):
            sys.exit(f"wake: --slot is lowercase letters, digits and dashes, not {args.slot!r}")
        sc["slot"] = args.slot
    if args.prompt:
        sc["prompt"] = args.prompt
    elif AGENT != LOCAL_AGENT:
        if not re.fullmatch(r"[A-Za-z0-9._/-]{1,200}\.md", args.prompt_file) or ".." in args.prompt_file.split("/"):
            sys.exit(f"wake: a lane file is a path in your repo, like routines/x.md, not {args.prompt_file}")
        sc["lane"] = args.prompt_file
    else:
        pf = Path(args.prompt_file)
        pf = pf if pf.is_absolute() else REPO / pf
        if origin and lane_file(pf) is None:
            sys.exit(f"wake: a wake from {origin} takes a lane file in the repo ({lane_dirs_text()}), not {args.prompt_file}")
        if not pf.is_file():
            sys.exit(f"wake: no such prompt file: {pf}")
        sc["prompt_file"] = str(pf)
    with Spool() as spool:
        # It replaces its own pending occurrence, and any one-off wake for the same lane
        # (a lane that re-armed itself before it had a schedule).
        for e in [e for e in spool.entries if e.get("schedule") == args.name
                  or (sc.get("prompt_file") and e["kind"] == "wake" and e.get("prompt_file") == sc["prompt_file"])]:
            disarm_timer(e["id"])
            spool.entries.remove(e)
            log("schedule-replaces", f"{args.name}: {e['id']}")
        for dm in [e for e in spool.entries if e["kind"] == "deadman"]:
            disarm_timer(dm["id"])
            spool.entries.remove(dm)
        scheds[args.name] = sc
        save_schedules(scheds)
        entry = schedule_entry(args.name, sc, next_occurrence(sc, datetime.now()))
        spool.entries.append(entry)
        arm_timer(entry)
    log("schedule-set", f"{args.name}: {sc['at']} {sc.get('days', 'daily')}, next {entry['id']} at {entry['at']}")
    print(f"schedule {args.name}: next at {entry['at']} ({entry['id']})")


def load_lanes():
    try:
        return json.loads(LANES.read_text())
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return {}


def save_lanes(lanes):
    LANES.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    tmp = LANES.with_suffix(".tmp")
    tmp.write_text(json.dumps(lanes, indent=1, sort_keys=True))
    tmp.replace(LANES)


def lane_prompt(name, lane):
    """What the assignee's house is handed: who the work is for, then the lane (or, too long for a house's task,
    where to read it). A lane that needs loom's machine says so, and runs there."""
    head = (f"This is a loom lane: household work on a schedule (\"{name}\"), assigned to you; the owner reassigns it "
            f"on loom's Clock page. Do it as yourself.\n\n")
    body = lane["text"] if len(lane["text"]) <= LANE_INLINE_MAX else (
        f"The lane's text is too long to hand over here: read it with `wake lane text {name}` "
        f"(in a house, `wake` reaches loom's clock piece) and follow it exactly, as if it were this prompt.")
    return ("<!-- house: local -->\n" if lane.get("local") else "") + head + body


def cmd_lane(args):
    """Loom lanes: set (create, replace, or move to another agent), assign, rm, list, text."""
    lanes = load_lanes()
    origin = os.environ.get("WAKE_ORIGIN", "").strip()
    if args.action == "list":
        if not lanes:
            print("no loom lanes")
        for name, ln in sorted(lanes.items()):
            when = when_text(ln)
            print(f"{name:<22} {ln['agent']:<8} {when:<18} {len(ln['text'])} chars{' local' if ln.get('local') else ''}" + (f"  — {ln['note']}" if ln.get("note") else ""))
        return
    if not SCHEDULE_NAME.match(args.name or ""):
        sys.exit("wake: a lane's name is lowercase letters, digits and dashes, like weekly-review")
    if args.action == "text":
        ln = lanes.get(args.name)
        if not ln:
            sys.exit(f"wake: no loom lane {args.name}")
        # Through the API an agent reads only a lane assigned to it.
        if origin.startswith("agent:") and origin != f"agent:{ln['agent']}":
            sys.exit(f"wake: {args.name} isn't assigned to you")
        sys.stdout.write(ln["text"] if ln["text"].endswith("\n") else ln["text"] + "\n")
        return
    if origin:
        sys.exit("wake: loom lanes are the owner's to set, assign and remove")
    if args.action == "rm":
        ln = lanes.pop(args.name, None)
        if not ln:
            sys.exit(f"wake: no loom lane {args.name}")
        configure(ln["agent"])
        if args.name in load_schedules():
            cmd_schedule(argparse.Namespace(action="rm", name=args.name))
        save_lanes(lanes)
        print(f"removed loom lane {args.name}")
        return
    if args.action == "assign":
        if args.name not in lanes:
            sys.exit(f"wake: no loom lane {args.name}")
        ln = dict(lanes[args.name])
    else:
        ln = dict(lanes.get(args.name) or {})
        if args.at:
            ln["at"] = [t.strip() for t in args.at.split(",")]
            ln["at"] = ln["at"][0] if len(ln["at"]) == 1 else ln["at"]
        if args.days is not None:
            ln["days"] = args.days.lower()
        if args.prompt or args.prompt_file:
            if bool(args.prompt) == bool(args.prompt_file):
                sys.exit("wake: a lane's text is --prompt/-p or --prompt-file/-f, not both")
            text = args.prompt
            if args.prompt_file:
                pf = Path(args.prompt_file)
                pf = pf if pf.is_absolute() else REPO / pf
                if not pf.is_file():
                    sys.exit(f"wake: no such lane file: {pf}")
                text = pf.read_text()
                ln["source"] = str(pf.resolve())
            else:
                ln.pop("source", None)
            ln["text"] = text
        for k in ("note", "model", "slot"):
            if getattr(args, k, ""):
                ln[k] = getattr(args, k)
        if ln.get("slot") and not SLOT_NAME.match(ln["slot"]):
            sys.exit(f"wake: --slot is lowercase letters, digits and dashes, not {ln['slot']!r}")
        if args.local is not None:
            ln["local"] = args.local
        if not ln.get("at") or not ln.get("text"):
            sys.exit("wake: a new loom lane needs --at and its text (-p or -f)")
    agent = getattr(args, "lane_agent", None) or ln.get("agent")
    if not agent or not AGENT_NAME.match(agent) or agent not in clock_agents() + [a for a in household_agents()]:
        sys.exit(f"wake: assign a loom lane to an agent of this household (--agent), not {agent!r}")
    # Moving it: off the old assignee's clock first.
    old = lanes.get(args.name, {}).get("agent")
    if old and old != agent:
        configure(old)
        if args.name in load_schedules():
            cmd_schedule(argparse.Namespace(action="rm", name=args.name))
    ln["agent"] = agent
    ln["updated"] = datetime.now().strftime(TIME_FMT)
    lanes[args.name] = ln
    save_lanes(lanes)
    configure(agent)
    at = ln["at"] if isinstance(ln["at"], str) else ",".join(ln["at"])
    cmd_schedule(argparse.Namespace(action="set", name=args.name, at=at, days=ln.get("days"), prompt=lane_prompt(args.name, ln),
                                    prompt_file=None, note=f"loom lane{': ' + ln['note'] if ln.get('note') else ''}",
                                    model=ln.get("model") or DEFAULT_MODEL, slot=ln.get("slot", "")))
    scheds = load_schedules()
    scheds[args.name]["loom_lane"] = True
    if ln.get("source"):
        scheds[args.name]["lane_file"] = ln["source"]
    save_schedules(scheds)
    # A one-off wake the lane armed for itself (its "re-arm yourself") is the schedule's to run now.
    if ln.get("source"):
        with Spool() as spool:
            for e in [e for e in spool.entries if e["kind"] == "wake" and e.get("prompt_file")
                      and Path(e["prompt_file"]).resolve() == Path(ln["source"])]:
                disarm_timer(e["id"])
                spool.entries.remove(e)
                log("lane-replaces", f"{args.name}: {e['id']}")
    print(f"loom lane {args.name}: {name_of(agent)}'s, {when_text(ln)}" + (" (on loom's machine)" if ln.get("local") else ""))


def household_agents():
    try:
        return [a for a in json.loads(HOUSEHOLD.read_text()).get("agents", []) if AGENT_NAME.match(a)]
    except (OSError, ValueError, AttributeError):
        return []


def cmd_cancel(args):
    with Spool() as spool:
        match = [e for e in spool.entries if e["id"] == args.id]
        if not match:
            sys.exit(f"wake: no spool entry {args.id}")
        spool.entries.remove(match[0])
        disarm_timer(args.id)
        # Cancelling one occurrence of a schedule skips just that one.
        sc = load_schedules().get(match[0].get("schedule") or "")
        if sc:
            at = datetime.strptime(match[0]["at"], TIME_FMT)
            nxt = schedule_entry(match[0]["schedule"], sc, next_occurrence(sc, max(at, datetime.now())))
            spool.entries.append(nxt)
            arm_timer(nxt)
            log("schedule-skip", f"{match[0]['schedule']}: skipped {args.id}, next {nxt['id']} at {nxt['at']}")
        ensure_deadman(spool)
    log("cancel", args.id)
    print(f"cancelled {args.id}")


def cmd_rearm(args):
    # At boot (the piece's `run` service, or a plain `wake rearm`) every clock comes back,
    # not only the local agent's: the timers are transient, and another agent's lanes would stop silently.
    every = getattr(args, "every", False)
    for agent in (clock_agents() if every else [AGENT]):
        if every:
            configure(agent)
        with Spool() as spool:
            for e in spool.entries:
                print(f"{agent} {e['id']}: {arm_timer(e)}")
            ensure_deadman(spool)
        log("rearm", f"{len(spool.entries)} entries")


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the bundle
# loom's household bundle (loom docs/extensions.md, "The bundle: a piece's part"):
# every agent's clock (its spool, schedules, pause and filed local-wake words) and loom's lanes, encrypted
# by this piece to the owner's recipients. Logs stay behind. Plaintext only on pipes.
BUNDLE_FORMAT = "loom-clock/1"
CLOCK_FILES = ("spool.jsonl", "schedules.json", "paused", "filed.json")


def age_bin():
    return os.environ.get("LOOM_AGE") or "age"


def cmd_bundle(args):
    if args.action == "export":
        recipients = [r.strip() for r in os.environ.get("LOOM_EXPORT_RECIPIENTS", "").split(",") if r.strip()]
        if not recipients:
            sys.exit("wake: LOOM_EXPORT_RECIPIENTS is empty: a part is never written out in the clear")
        clocks = {}
        for agent in clock_agents():
            configure(agent)
            files = {f: (WAKE_DIR / f).read_text() for f in CLOCK_FILES if (WAKE_DIR / f).is_file()}
            if files:
                clocks[agent] = files
        doc = json.dumps({"format": BUNDLE_FORMAT, "clocks": clocks, "lanes": LANES.read_text() if LANES.is_file() else "",
                          "fire": FIRE_CONF.read_text().strip() if FIRE_CONF.is_file() else ""})
        r = subprocess.run([age_bin(), "-e", "-a", *[x for rcp in recipients for x in ("-r", rcp)]],
                           input=doc, capture_output=True, text=True)
        if r.returncode != 0:
            sys.exit(f"wake: age: {r.stderr.strip()[-200:]}")
        sys.stdout.write(r.stdout)
        return
    identity = os.environ.get("LOOM_IMPORT_IDENTITY", "")
    if not identity:
        sys.exit("wake: LOOM_IMPORT_IDENTITY names the owner's key file")
    r = subprocess.run([age_bin(), "-d", "-i", identity], input=sys.stdin.read(), capture_output=True, text=True)
    if r.returncode != 0:
        sys.exit("wake: the part doesn't decrypt with LOOM_IMPORT_IDENTITY. Nothing was written.")
    try:
        doc = json.loads(r.stdout)
    except ValueError:
        doc = None
    if not isinstance(doc, dict) or doc.get("format") != BUNDLE_FORMAT or not isinstance(doc.get("clocks"), dict):
        sys.exit(f"wake: the part decrypts but isn't a {BUNDLE_FORMAT} part. Nothing was written.")
    agents = [a for a in doc["clocks"] if AGENT_NAME.match(a)]
    if not args.force:
        for a in agents:
            configure(a)
            if any((WAKE_DIR / f).exists() for f in CLOCK_FILES):
                sys.exit(f"wake: {a}'s clock is already here; restore onto a fresh one, or pass --force. Nothing was written.")
    for a in agents:
        configure(a)
        WAKE_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        for f in CLOCK_FILES:
            body = doc["clocks"][a].get(f)
            if isinstance(body, str):
                (WAKE_DIR / f).write_text(body)
    # An older part's relay log ("relays") is left out: relays are the runtime's now.
    # The household's loom lanes (their schedules came back in the assignees' clocks).
    if doc.get("lanes") and (args.force or not LANES.exists()):
        LANES.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        LANES.write_text(doc["lanes"])
    # The clock's mode (local, house, mixed), where this machine has none of its own.
    if doc.get("fire") in ("local", "house", "mixed") and not FIRE_CONF.exists():
        FIRE_CONF.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        FIRE_CONF.write_text(doc["fire"] + "\n")
    # Quiet until the owner says: a restored clock is paused (held wakes fire once each on
    # resume). The old machine may still be up, and this one holds live credentials: two
    # clocks firing the same lanes would do every job twice.
    for a in agents:
        configure(a)
        if not PAUSED.exists():
            PAUSED.write_text(json.dumps({"since": datetime.now().strftime(TIME_FMT), "by": "restore"}))
    # The timers are this machine's: arm every restored clock's wakes here.
    cmd_rearm(argparse.Namespace(every=True))
    print(f"restored {len(agents)} clock(s), paused: {', '.join(agents)}. When this is the machine that "
          f"should act: wake --agent <name> resume")


def paused():
    """{since, by} while this clock is paused, else None."""
    try:
        return json.loads(PAUSED.read_text())
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None


def cmd_pause(_args):
    if paused():
        print(f"{AGENT}'s clock is already paused")
        return
    WAKE_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    PAUSED.write_text(json.dumps({"since": datetime.now().strftime(TIME_FMT), "by": os.environ.get("WAKE_BY", "")}))
    log("pause", os.environ.get("WAKE_BY", ""))
    print(f"paused {AGENT}'s clock: wakes that come due are held until resume")


def cmd_resume(_args):
    """Unpause; every held wake fires once, in order, a minute apart."""
    if not paused():
        print(f"{AGENT}'s clock isn't paused")
        return
    with Spool() as spool:
        held = sorted((e for e in spool.entries if e.get("held")), key=lambda e: e["at"])
        for i, e in enumerate(held):
            del e["held"]
            # our timer for the old id was collected when it fired; a fresh id anyway
            e["id"] = "w-" + secrets.token_hex(3)
            e["at"] = (datetime.now() + timedelta(minutes=1 + i)).strftime(TIME_FMT)
            arm_timer(e)
        PAUSED.unlink(missing_ok=True)
    log("resume", f"{len(held)} held")
    print(f"resumed {AGENT}'s clock" + (f": {len(held)} held wake{'s' if len(held) != 1 else ''} fire from a minute from now" if held else ""))


def cmd_now(args):
    """A one-off wake a minute out, with no lane; it runs even while paused."""
    who = os.environ.get("WAKE_BY") or "the owner"
    entry = {"id": "w-" + secrets.token_hex(3), "kind": "wake", "now": True,
             "at": datetime.now().strftime(TIME_FMT), "note": args.note or "woken now from loom",
             "prompt": NOW_PROMPT.format(who=who), "model": DEFAULT_MODEL, "created": datetime.now().strftime(TIME_FMT),
             "for": "owner"}  # loom's page, on loom's machine (not a verb the piece API passes)
    with Spool() as spool:
        for dm in [e for e in spool.entries if e["kind"] == "deadman"]:
            disarm_timer(dm["id"])
            spool.entries.remove(dm)
        spool.entries.append(entry)
        arm_timer(entry)
    log("set", f"{entry['id']} at {entry['at']} note={entry['note']!r}")
    print(f"{entry['id']}: {AGENT} wakes within a minute")


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- relay
# Agent to agent moved to loom's runtime (loom docs/specs/agent-runtime.md, "Agent-to-agent relay"): a relay is a
# delivery on the runtime's `relay` venue, through its `relay` MCP tool or `loom runtime relay` from a house. Pairing
# is the runtime's permissions, and an unpaired relay's approval is spent there. The clock only says where it went.
RELAY_MOVED = ("wake: relays moved to loom's runtime: use the relay tool (to, say, why?, reply_to?, from?, approval?), "
               "or from a house: loom runtime relay --to <agent> --say \"…\" [--reply-to r-…] [--approval a-…]; "
               "loom runtime relays lists them")


def plain(text, n):
    """One short line that can't close the brief's header or start a line of its own."""
    t = unicodedata.normalize("NFKC", str(text or ""))
    t = "".join(" " if (unicodedata.category(c)[0] in "CZ" and c != " ") or unicodedata.category(c) in ("Ps", "Pe") else c for c in t)
    return re.sub(r" +", " ", t).strip()[:n]


def cmd_relay(args):
    sys.exit(RELAY_MOVED)


def file_approval(kind, target, what, why):
    """File an approval request (loom's approvals piece) for the body this runs for; its id, or None."""
    argv = [*approvals_argv(), "request", "--kind", kind, "--target", target, "--what", what, "--why", why]
    caller = os.environ.get("WAKE_CALLER", "").strip()
    if caller:
        # And on whose behalf (t-1943): the approval names them on its card and is spent only for them, so filing and
        # spending say the same (the caller's verified principal; "-" reads as someone loom can't name).
        argv += ["--as", caller, "--on-behalf", principal_for()]
    env = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if k != "HOUSE_ID"}
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(argv, capture_output=True, text=True, env=env, timeout=30)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as e:
        sys.exit(f"wake: couldn't ask the owner: the approvals piece didn't run ({e})")
    m = re.match(r"(a-[0-9a-f]{8}):", r.stdout or "")
    if r.returncode == 0 and m:
        return m.group(1)
    sys.exit(f"wake: couldn't ask the owner: {(r.stderr or r.stdout).strip()[-300:]}")


def spend_approval(aid, kind, target):
    """Spend an approval (loom's approvals piece) for the body this runs for: over the clock's
    piece API that's the caller loom named (WAKE_CALLER); run here, loom's machine.
    "" when spent, else the piece's reason."""
    argv = [*approvals_argv(), "use", aid, "--kind", kind, "--target", target]
    caller = os.environ.get("WAKE_CALLER", "").strip()
    if caller:
        # And on whose behalf (t-1943): the approval names them on its card and is spent only for them, so filing and
        # spending say the same (the caller's verified principal; "-" reads as someone loom can't name).
        argv += ["--as", caller, "--on-behalf", principal_for()]
    env = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if k != "HOUSE_ID"}
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(argv, capture_output=True, text=True, env=env, timeout=30)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as e:
        return f"the approvals piece didn't run ({e})"
    # The piece's reason, not just no: "isn't allowed" alone hides "asked in another house",
    # and a body can spend hours hunting a mismatch that isn't there.
    return "" if r.returncode == 0 else ((r.stderr or r.stdout).strip()[-300:] or f"exit {r.returncode}")


def cmd_relays(args):
    sys.exit(RELAY_MOVED)


HOUSE_READY = "<!-- house: ready -->"
HOUSE_LOCAL = "<!-- house: local -->"
LOCAL_WAKE_MAX = 270   # a local wake's whole prompt fits on the owner's card (approvals' 300, less its prefix)
# A lane's own bookkeeping (last-run stamps, cursors): `<!-- house-slot: nightly -->`
# in its first 30 lines names the loom-box slot its house restores and saves.
HOUSE_SLOT = re.compile(r"^<!-- house-slot: ([a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,39}) -->$")


def fire_mode():
    m = os.environ.get("WAKE_FIRE", "").strip()
    if not m:
        try:
            m = FIRE_CONF.read_text().strip()
        except OSError:
            m = ""
    return m if m in ("house", "mixed") else "local"


def house_slot(entry, body):
    """The slot a lane's house keeps its bookkeeping in, if its file names one."""
    if "prompt_file" not in entry:
        return None
    for line in body.splitlines()[:30]:
        m = HOUSE_SLOT.match(line.strip())
        if m:
            return m.group(1)
    return None


def house_ready(entry, body):
    """Whether a wake runs in a house (fire mode "mixed"). A lane file says so itself
    (`<!-- house: ready -->` in its first 30 lines). An inline prompt does unless it says it
    needs loom's machine (`<!-- house: local -->`): most follow-ups need nothing a house lacks."""
    if "prompt_file" in entry:
        return any(l.strip() == HOUSE_READY for l in body.splitlines()[:30])
    return HOUSE_LOCAL not in body


def local_run():
    """How a wake that runs here runs (WAKE_LOCAL_RUN): "runtime" (the default, t-1921): delivered, and loom's runtime
    runs its body here; "session": the session command here, the old way (and the way back)."""
    return "session" if setting("WAKE_LOCAL_RUN").strip().lower() == "session" else "runtime"


# The session a local wake starts the old way: {prompt} and {model} are filled in (a whole argument each).
# Safe by default: a session that can stop and ask. An agent that runs unattended and has decided to skip permission
# prompts sets WAKE_SESSION_COMMAND itself, so that choice is written down where it's made.
SESSION_DEFAULT = ["claude", "--bg", "{prompt}", "--model", "{model}"]


def session_argv(prompt, model):
    return [{"{prompt}": prompt, "{model}": model}.get(a, a) for a in argv_setting("WAKE_SESSION_COMMAND", SESSION_DEFAULT)]


def dispatch(prompt, model, env, mode, agent=None, slot=None):
    """Start the wake's session; returns the CompletedProcess."""
    agent = agent or LOCAL_AGENT
    cwd = REPO if REPO.is_dir() else HOME
    try:
        if mode == "house":
            # The house reads its task as JSON: the prompt and the model it runs on.
            # loom-box puts it on the agent's primary box.
            task = json.dumps({"prompt": prompt, "model": model})
            return subprocess.run([LOOM, "box", "up", "--agent", agent, *(["--slot", slot] if slot else []), "--task", "-"],
                                  input=task, capture_output=True, text=True, cwd=cwd, env=env)
        return subprocess.run(session_argv(prompt, model), capture_output=True, text=True, cwd=cwd, env=env)
    except OSError as e:
        # A command that isn't there is a failed dispatch like any other: retried, then said.
        return subprocess.CompletedProcess(args=[], returncode=127, stdout="", stderr=str(e))


RETRY_ALERT_AT = 3
# loom-box's refusal when a house already holds the slot (src/control.mjs).
SLOT_BUSY = re.compile(r"holds \S+ \S+ slot; one house at a time")
RETRY_GIVE_UP = 6
# A house handed to loom-box isn't a house started: it's looked at again this long
# after, and while it still hasn't started, this many times before it's said once.
WATCH_AFTER = timedelta(minutes=10)
WATCH_CHECKS = 6
HOUSE_ID = re.compile(r"^(h-\d+):")


def alert(msg):
    """Reach the owner without a model session: WAKE_ALERT_COMMAND with the message as its last
    argument (a chat webhook, a push). Always in the clock's log; never fails the caller."""
    log("alert", msg)
    cmd = argv_setting("WAKE_ALERT_COMMAND", [])
    if not cmd:
        return
    try:
        subprocess.run([*cmd, msg], capture_output=True, timeout=30)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        pass


def alert_daily(key, msg):
    """alert(), at most once a day for one key (a stamp in the agent's clock dir); always logged."""
    stamp = WAKE_DIR / f"alerted-{key}"
    try:
        if time.time() - stamp.stat().st_mtime < 86400:
            log("alert-quiet", msg)
            return
    except OSError:
        pass
    try:
        WAKE_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        stamp.write_text(datetime.now().strftime(TIME_FMT) + "\n")
    except OSError:
        pass
    alert(msg)


def fire_gate_open():
    """WAKE_FIRE_GATE: a command that says whether this machine should dispatch now (exit 0), for a
    standby that mirrors a primary and must never run the same lanes. No gate: always open."""
    cmd = argv_setting("WAKE_FIRE_GATE", [])
    if not cmd:
        return True
    try:
        return subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, timeout=60).returncode == 0
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return False


# ─── Delivery (loom docs/specs/agent-runtime.md, "5. Delivery") ─────────────
# A wake is delivered, not started: the clock hands it to loom's `deliver` with its own piece token, and the runtime
# writes the wake's turn and reaches the agent's body. The clock names no harness and no house here.
DELIVER_TIMEOUT_S = 130   # core forwards for up to 120 s
DELIVER_TEXT_MAX = 40000
DELIVER_ID_MAX = 200
DELIVER_LABEL_MAX = 80
BODY_STATES = ("fed", "resumed", "started", "queued")
NO_DELIVERY = "no installed piece offers delivery"


def delivery_mode():
    """"deliver" or "spawn" (WAKE_DELIVERY). Unset: "deliver" when the clock has a token to deliver with (core then
    says whether a piece offers delivery; with none, that wake falls back to "spawn"), else "spawn"."""
    m = setting("WAKE_DELIVERY").strip().lower()
    if m in ("spawn", "deliver"):
        return m
    return "auto" if setting("WAKE_DELIVER_TOKEN_FILE") else "spawn"


def loom_api():
    """loom's address for its HTTP API (WAKE_LOOM_URL; an MCP URL's /mcp is dropped)."""
    u = (setting("WAKE_LOOM_URL") or os.environ.get("LOOM_URL") or "http://127.0.0.1:8787").rstrip("/")
    return u[:-4] if u.endswith("/mcp") else u


PLACE = re.compile(r"[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}:[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._@:/-]{0,159}")


def wake_place(entry, local=False):
    """Where a wake lands in the agent's conversations (conversations.md: one per agent, venue and place). A lane's
    wakes share one, so a lane's runs read as one conversation and its body can resume: `lane:<name>`, by the
    schedule, else the lane file; `local-lane:<name>` for its runs on loom's machine (a conversation's bodies run in
    one place, and a lane can move). Anything else is its own: `wake:<id>`, by the id it was first fired under."""
    if entry.get("deliver_place"):
        return entry["deliver_place"]
    if entry.get("place"):
        return entry["place"]
    name = entry.get("schedule")
    if not name and (entry.get("lane") or entry.get("prompt_file")):
        name = Path(entry.get("lane") or entry["prompt_file"]).stem
    if name:
        return f"{'local-lane' if local else 'lane'}:{name}"[:200]
    return f"wake:{entry['id']}"


def wake_label(entry):
    what = entry.get("note") or (pretty(entry["schedule"]) if entry.get("schedule") else "") or entry["id"]
    return plain(what, DELIVER_LABEL_MAX) or entry["id"]


def post_delivery(body):
    """POST /api/loom/deliver: (status, answer). 0 is no answer (loom down, a timeout, no token)."""
    tf = setting("WAKE_DELIVER_TOKEN_FILE")
    try:
        token = Path(tf).expanduser().read_text().strip() if tf else ""
    except OSError as e:
        return 0, {"error": f"can't read WAKE_DELIVER_TOKEN_FILE: {e.strerror}"}
    if not token:
        return 0, {"error": "no token to deliver with (WAKE_DELIVER_TOKEN_FILE: a piece token of this clock's)"}
    req = urllib.request.Request(f"{loom_api()}/api/loom/deliver", data=json.dumps(body).encode(), method="POST",
                                 headers={"content-type": "application/json", "authorization": f"Bearer {token}"})
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=DELIVER_TIMEOUT_S) as r:
            raw, status = r.read(), r.status
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:
        raw, status = e.read(), e.code
    except (urllib.error.URLError, OSError, ValueError) as e:
        return 0, {"error": f"loom didn't answer: {getattr(e, 'reason', e)}"}
    try:
        ans = json.loads(raw or b"{}")
    except ValueError:
        ans = {}
    return status, ans if isinstance(ans, dict) else {}


def as_retry(entry):
    """A schedule's run that didn't go is retried as a one-off: its next occurrence is already armed."""
    if entry.get("kind") == "schedule":
        entry["kind"] = "wake"
        entry["note"] = f"retry of {entry.pop('schedule')}: {entry.get('note', '')}"


def deliver_wake(entry, prompt, agent, auto, local=False):
    """Deliver one wake. Answers "spawn" when it should go the old way after all (auto, and loom has no piece
    offering delivery), else None, having logged what came of it:
      - an answer (fed, resumed, started, queued): logged, done; the runtime has it from here;
      - failed: the turn stands and no body took it: retried later as a new delivery (a new id, the same place);
      - no answer, a 5xx or a 429: retried later with the same id and body, which loom answers once;
      - any other refusal (400, 403, 409, 413): said loudly, never retried: a retry would be refused the same way."""
    body = entry.get("delivery")
    if not body:
        # A local wake says so in the contract's own field (`local: true`), never by the words: its marker is this
        # clock's input syntax only, and goes. The runtime trusts the field from this piece alone.
        text = prompt.replace(HOUSE_LOCAL, "").strip() if local else prompt
        body = {"id": entry["id"][:DELIVER_ID_MAX], "agent": agent, "venue": "wake", "place": wake_place(entry, local),
                "label": wake_label(entry), "from": {"kind": "schedule"}, "kind": "wake",
                "at": datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.000Z"), "text": text[:DELIVER_TEXT_MAX],
                **({"local": True} if local else {})}
    # Whom it's for, handed to the runtime before the delivery it belongs to (t-1943). Not fatal: without it the
    # runtime treats the wake as unknown. (A wake that goes the old way, a spawned house or a session here, has no
    # runtime record to hand it to: there it's unknown.)
    hand_over_principal(agent, body["place"], body["id"], entry_for(entry))
    status, ans = post_delivery(body)
    err = str(ans.get("error") or ans.get("reason") or "")[:200]
    if auto and status == 503 and NO_DELIVERY in err:
        log("fire-spawn", f"{entry['id']} {err}: sent the old way")
        return "spawn"
    if local and (status in (400, 403) or (status == 503 and NO_DELIVERY in err)):
        # A wake for loom's machine that the runtime won't run here (no local bodies for this agent): a session here,
        # as before, so it still runs where it needs to; only its conversation is lost. Said once a day: every wake
        # here is the runtime's now (t-1921), and one that isn't is a setting to fix, not a way to keep running.
        log("fire-spawn", f"{entry['id']} deliver to {body['place']} refused ({status}: {err}): a session here instead")
        alert_daily("local-refused", f"wake: loom's runtime won't run wakes on loom's machine ({status}: {err}), so the clock "
                    f"starts them as sessions itself, as before t-1921. Fix LOOM_RUNTIME_LOCAL_BODIES, or set "
                    f"WAKE_LOCAL_RUN=session to say so")
        return "spawn"
    # What every retry keeps: the conversation it belongs to.
    entry["deliver_place"], entry["deliver_label"] = body["place"], body["label"]
    via = "" if body["id"] == entry["id"] else f" as {body['id']}"
    if status == 200 and ans.get("body") in BODY_STATES:
        why = f" ({str(ans['reason'])[:120]})" if ans.get("reason") else ""
        log("fire", f"{entry['id']} delivered{via}: {ans['body']}{why}, {ans.get('conversation')} seq {ans.get('seq')}")
        return None
    entry.pop("delivery", None)
    as_retry(entry)
    if status == 200 and ans.get("body") == "failed":
        # loom keeps that answer a day: the same id would only be told `failed` again. A new delivery, same place.
        retry(entry, f"delivered{via} but no body took it: {err or 'failed'}", "fire-fail")
        return None
    if status in (0, 429) or status >= 500:
        entry["delivery"] = body
        retry(entry, f"deliver{via}: {status or 'no answer'} {err}", "fire-fail")
        return None
    log("fire-refused", f"{entry['id']} deliver{via} REFUSED {status}: {err}; not retried")
    alert(f"wake: loom refused to deliver \"{entry.get('note') or entry['id']}\" ({status}): {err}. Not retried: fix the "
          f"clock's settings or the wake, or set WAKE_DELIVERY=spawn")
    return None


def cmd_fire(args):
    # The fire gate (one writer): a standby never dispatches a lane.
    # Keep the entry, push it out an hour, re-check then.
    if not fire_gate_open():
        with Spool() as spool:
            for e in spool.entries:
                if e["id"] == args.id:
                    # our own unit name is still loaded (we ARE it) — re-arm under a fresh id
                    old_id, e["id"] = e["id"], "w-" + secrets.token_hex(3)
                    e["at"] = (datetime.now() + timedelta(hours=1)).strftime(TIME_FMT)
                    arm_timer(e)
                    log("fire-standby", f"{old_id} not prime — deferred as {e['id']} at {e['at']}")
        return
    with Spool() as spool:
        match = [e for e in spool.entries if e["id"] == args.id]
        if not match:
            log("fire-miss", args.id)
            return  # cancelled between arm and fire — nothing to do
        entry = match[0]
        # A watch is a check, not work: a pause doesn't hold it.
        if paused() and not entry.get("now") and entry.get("kind") != "watch":
            # Held, not lost: it stays in the spool and fires once on resume.
            entry["held"] = True
            log("fire-held", f"{entry['id']} paused")
            return
        spool.entries.remove(entry)
        ensure_deadman(spool)
    if entry.get("kind") == "watch":
        watch_house(entry)
        return
    if entry.get("kind") == "parked":
        state = request_state(entry["on"])
        if state == "pending" and datetime.now() < datetime.strptime(entry["until"], TIME_FMT):
            # Still waiting: check again later; no body runs for it.
            entry["id"], entry["at"] = "w-" + secrets.token_hex(3), (datetime.now() + PARK_CHECK).strftime(TIME_FMT)
            with Spool() as spool:
                spool.entries.append(entry)
                arm_timer(entry)
            return
        log("unpark", f"{entry['id']} {entry['on']} {state}")
        unpark(entry, state)
    origin = entry.get("origin")
    if entry.get("kind") == "schedule":
        # The schedule's next occurrence first: the chain doesn't depend on this run.
        with Spool() as spool:
            sc = load_schedules().get(entry.get("schedule"))
            if sc and not any(e.get("schedule") == entry["schedule"] for e in spool.entries):
                nxt = schedule_entry(entry["schedule"], sc, next_occurrence(sc, datetime.now() + timedelta(minutes=1)))
                spool.entries.append(nxt)
                arm_timer(nxt)
                log("schedule-next", f"{entry['schedule']}: {nxt['id']} at {nxt['at']}")
    if "lane" in entry:
        body = (f"Your lane for this wake is the file `{entry['lane']}` in your own repo (your house's "
                f"checkout). Read it and follow it.")
    elif "prompt_file" in entry:
        if origin and lane_file(entry["prompt_file"]) is None:
            log("fire-refused", f"{entry['id']} from {origin}: {entry['prompt_file']} is no longer a lane file")
            return
        body = Path(entry["prompt_file"]).read_text()
    else:
        body = entry["prompt"]
    note = f", note: {entry['note']}" if entry.get("note") else ""
    # An agent's own wake never runs as a session on loom's machine.
    # Another agent's clock, or an agent's own wake: always a house, never a session here.
    mode = "house" if origin or AGENT != LOCAL_AGENT else fire_mode()
    if entry.get("local_approval") and AGENT == LOCAL_AGENT:
        mode = "local"  # the owner allowed this one wake on loom's machine (cmd_set)
    if mode == "mixed":
        mode = "house" if house_ready(entry, body) else "local"
    # A slot the wake names (wake --slot, an agent's lanes), else one its lane file names.
    slot = (entry.get("slot") or house_slot(entry, body)) if mode == "house" else None
    if mode == "house" and "prompt_file" in entry:
        # The house has the repo: it gets the lane's path, not its text.
        # loom-box takes a task of 8000 characters at most, and many lanes
        # are longer: handed their text, every run (and retry) would fail.
        pf = Path(entry["prompt_file"])
        rel = pf.relative_to(REPO) if pf.is_absolute() and pf.is_relative_to(REPO) else pf
        body = (f"Your lane for this wake is the file `{rel}` in your own repo (your house's "
                f"checkout). Read it and follow it.")
    # Delivered: a wake for the agent's house that needs no house slot (delivery keeps a conversation, not a slot). A
    # wake for loom's machine is delivered too (t-1921): the runtime runs its body here, when it runs local bodies for
    # this agent; else it's a session here, as before. A house's wake the owner allowed here is one of them: its own
    # `wake:<id>` (it can't name a place). WAKE_LOCAL_RUN=session: only one set here that names its place (t-1830).
    local_place = mode == "local" and AGENT == LOCAL_AGENT and (
        local_run() == "runtime" or (bool(entry.get("place")) and not origin and not entry.get("local_approval")))
    dmode = delivery_mode() if (mode == "house" or local_place) and not slot else "spawn"

    def prompt_for(where):
        # The preamble is the agent's (WAKE_PREAMBLE_FILE): it goes in the wake's text, since it carries this
        # wake's own id, note and time, and the runtime hands a wake's text to the body as it came.
        try:
            return preamble_template().format(name=name_of(AGENT), where=where, id=entry["id"], kind=entry["kind"],
                                              created=entry["created"], note=note, body=body, lanes=lane_dir())
        except (KeyError, IndexError, ValueError) as e:
            log("preamble", f"WAKE_PREAMBLE_FILE doesn't format ({e}); the piece's own is used")
            return PREAMBLE.format(name=name_of(AGENT), where=where, id=entry["id"], kind=entry["kind"],
                                   created=entry["created"], note=note, body=body, lanes=lane_dir())

    agent = origin.split(":", 1)[1] if origin else AGENT
    if dmode != "spawn":
        where = "on loom's machine (loom's runtime delivered it)" if local_place else "in your house (loom's runtime delivered it)"
        if deliver_wake(entry, prompt_for(where), agent, dmode == "auto", local=local_place) != "spawn":
            return
    where = "in a fresh house (loom-box)" if mode == "house" else "on loom's machine"
    prompt = prompt_for(where)
    env = os.environ.copy()
    prepend = ":".join(
        p for p in [str(HOME / ".local" / "bin"), str(REPO / "bin")]
        if p not in env.get("PATH", "").split(":") and Path(p).is_dir()
    )
    if prepend:
        env["PATH"] = prepend + (":" + env["PATH"] if env.get("PATH") else "")
    r = dispatch(prompt, entry.get("model", DEFAULT_MODEL), env, mode, agent, slot)
    if r.returncode != 0:
        # Dispatch failed: put the wake back under a fresh id — our own unit
        # name is still loaded (we ARE it, same as the fire-gate branch
        # above) so re-arming under entry["id"] unchanged collides with
        # ourselves: systemd-run refuses the name, and the retry would
        # vanish. A fresh id sidesteps the collision entirely.
        if entry.get("kind") == "schedule" and SLOT_BUSY.search(r.stderr or ""):
            # Its slot is held, most likely by this lane's own earlier run, and its
            # next occurrence is already armed: nothing to retry. (A schedule that runs
            # every 15 minutes would otherwise start a retry chain, and alerts, per try.)
            log("fire-busy", f"{entry['id']} {r.stderr.strip()[:200]} — skipped; next occurrence is armed")
            return
        # Its next occurrence is already armed: the retry is a one-off.
        as_retry(entry)
        # A wake that keeps failing backs off, says so once, and gives up,
        # rather than failing every 15 minutes with nobody hearing of it.
        retry(entry, f"rc={r.returncode} {r.stderr.strip()[:200]}", "fire-fail")
        sys.exit(1)
    out = r.stdout.strip()
    # One line: `claude --bg` adds a few lines of help after its `backgrounded · <id>`.
    log("fire", f"{entry['id']} {(out.splitlines() or [''])[0][:120]}")
    if mode != "house":
        job = SESSION_JOB.search(out)
        if job:
            record_session(job.group(1), entry)
    m = HOUSE_ID.match(out) if mode == "house" else None
    if m:
        # Handed over isn't started: look at the house again in a while.
        arm_watch(m.group(1), entry, 0)


def retry(entry, err, event):
    """A wake that didn't get going: back again with back-off, said at the third, given up at the sixth."""
    fails = entry["fails"] = entry.get("fails", 0) + 1
    what = entry.get("note") or entry.get("prompt_file") or entry["id"]
    if fails >= RETRY_GIVE_UP:
        log("fire-giveup", f"{entry['id']} {err} — failed {fails} times, not retried")
        alert(f"wake gave up on \"{what}\" after {fails} failures in a row: {err}")
        return
    if fails == RETRY_ALERT_AT:
        alert(f"wake: \"{what}\" has failed {fails} times in a row: {err}. Retrying with back-off; "
              f"it gives up after {RETRY_GIVE_UP}.")
    old_id, entry["id"] = entry["id"], "w-" + secrets.token_hex(3)
    entry["at"] = (datetime.now() + timedelta(minutes=15 * 2 ** (fails - 1))).strftime(TIME_FMT)
    with Spool() as spool:
        for dm in [e for e in spool.entries if e["kind"] == "deadman"]:
            disarm_timer(dm["id"])
            spool.entries.remove(dm)
        spool.entries.append(entry)
        arm_timer(entry)
    log(event, f"{old_id} {err} — retry {fails} as {entry['id']} {entry['at']}")


def arm_watch(house, wake, checks):
    w = {"id": "w-" + secrets.token_hex(3), "kind": "watch", "at": (datetime.now() + WATCH_AFTER).strftime(TIME_FMT),
         "house": house, "checks": checks, "note": f"Checking that its house started: {short(what_of(wake)) or 'a wake'}",
         "created": datetime.now().strftime(TIME_FMT), "wake": wake}
    with Spool() as spool:
        spool.entries.append(w)
        arm_timer(w)


def house_record(house):
    """loom-box's record of a house, or None if it has none (or can't be asked)."""
    try:
        r = subprocess.run([LOOM, "box", "list", "--json"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60)
        d = json.loads(r.stdout)
    except (OSError, ValueError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return None
    houses = d.get("houses", []) if isinstance(d, dict) else d
    return next((h for h in houses if isinstance(h, dict) and h.get("id") == house), None)


def watch_house(entry):
    """A watch came due: did the house its wake was handed to ever start?"""
    h = house_record(entry["house"])
    wake = entry["wake"]
    if h is None or h.get("started"):
        # Gone from loom-box's list, or it started: from here it's the lane's own business.
        log("watch", f"{entry['house']} {'started' if h else 'not listed'}; {wake['id']} let go")
        return
    if h.get("state") in ("failed", "stopped"):
        retry(wake, f"{entry['house']} never started: {str(h.get('log') or h.get('state'))[-200:]}", "start-fail")
        return
    checks = entry.get("checks", 0) + 1
    if checks >= WATCH_CHECKS:
        alert(f"wake: {entry['house']} for \"{wake.get('note') or wake['id']}\" still hasn't started "
              f"({h.get('state')}) after {checks * WATCH_AFTER.seconds // 60} minutes; not watching it any longer")
        log("watch-giveup", f"{entry['house']} {h.get('state')} after {checks} checks")
        return
    arm_watch(entry["house"], wake, checks)


# ─── Stuck sessions (t-1854) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A session the clock started here runs with nobody at its terminal. When it stops on a permission prompt it waits
# forever: on 2026-11-04 seven sat 4 to 30 hours, each holding a few hundred MB, and the overnight checker read every
# one as a dead round. So the clock keeps a record of the sessions it started (sessions.json, by the id `claude --bg`
# prints), looks at them every REAP_CHECK seconds (`claude agents --json`), and one that has been waiting on a
# permission prompt for WAKE_STUCK_AFTER minutes, counted from when the clock first saw it waiting, is stopped
# (`claude stop`, which keeps its conversation), commented on its task, logged `stuck`, and said once. Only the
# sessions in that record are ever looked at: never an interactive session, never one anyone else started.
# The `stuck` line in wake.log: `<wake> session=<id> alerted=yes|no stopped=yes|no task=<t-N|none>
# comment=ok|failed|none waited=<N>m | <tool>: "<redacted excerpt>"` (or `| unknown` when the transcript can't be
# read). alerted says an alert command is configured, not that it was delivered (alert() never reports that).

SESSION_JOB = re.compile(r"^backgrounded · (\S+)", re.M)
SESSIONS_KEEP = timedelta(days=7)
REAP_CHECK = 120          # seconds between the service's looks at its sessions
STUCK_AFTER_DEFAULT = 10  # minutes
TASK_ID = re.compile(r"\bt-\d+\b")   # taskstore's ids, in a wake's note
CMD_SHOWN = 120   # characters of the command a comment or the log shows, after redact()
# A command can carry a credential, and task comments are read back by agents: what the clock shows of one goes
# through redact() first, and the alert shows none of it.
REDACTIONS = [
    (re.compile(r"(?i)\b(authorization|proxy-authorization)\s*[:=]\s*(?:(?:bearer|basic|token)\s+)?[^\s'\"]+"), r"\1: [redacted]"),
    (re.compile(r"(?i)\bbearer\s+[^\s'\"]+"), "Bearer [redacted]"),
    (re.compile(r"(?i)(\b[\w-]*(?:token|key|secret|password|passwd|pwd)[\w-]*\s*[=:]\s*)(?:\"[^\"]*\"|'[^']*'|[^\s&'\"]+)"), r"\1[redacted]"),
    (re.compile(r"(?i)(--[\w-]*(?:token|key|secret|password)[\w-]*[ =])(?:\"[^\"]*\"|'[^']*'|\S+)"), r"\1[redacted]"),
    (re.compile(r"\b(?:ghp|gho|ghu|ghs|ghr)_[A-Za-z0-9]{10,}|\bgithub_pat_[A-Za-z0-9_]{10,}|\bsk-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,}|\bxox[abposr]-[A-Za-z0-9-]{8,}"), "[redacted]"),
    (re.compile(r"(?i)\b([a-z][a-z0-9+.-]*://)[^/\s:@]+(?::[^/\s@]*)?@"), r"\1[redacted]@"),
    # A long run of base64 or hex: a token, unless it's plainly words (a kebab-case name like alert-upgrade-skip-…).
    (re.compile(r"[A-Za-z0-9+_=-]{24,}"), lambda m: m.group(0) if re.fullmatch(r"[a-z]+(?:-[a-z]+)+", m.group(0)) else "[redacted]"),
]


def redact(text):
    """Credentials out of a command before any of it is shown: auth headers, key=value secrets, known token
    prefixes, URL userinfo, and long base64/hex runs."""
    out = str(text)
    for rx, rep in REDACTIONS:
        out = rx.sub(rep, out)
    return out


def stuck_after():
    """WAKE_STUCK_AFTER: minutes a session may wait on a permission prompt (default 10; 0 or off: never stopped)."""
    raw = setting("WAKE_STUCK_AFTER", str(STUCK_AFTER_DEFAULT)).strip().lower()
    if raw in ("0", "off", "no", "never"):
        return None
    try:
        v = float(raw)
    except ValueError:
        return timedelta(minutes=STUCK_AFTER_DEFAULT)
    return timedelta(minutes=v) if v > 0 else None


class Sessions:
    """Locked read-modify-write access to the record of sessions this clock started."""

    def __enter__(self):
        WAKE_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        self.path = WAKE_DIR / "sessions.json"
        self._lock = open(WAKE_DIR / "sessions.lock", "w")
        fcntl.flock(self._lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        try:
            d = json.loads(self.path.read_text())
            self.records = d if isinstance(d, dict) else {}
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            self.records = {}
        return self

    def __exit__(self, *exc):
        tmp = self.path.with_suffix(".tmp")
        tmp.write_text(json.dumps(self.records, indent=1) + "\n")
        tmp.replace(self.path)
        fcntl.flock(self._lock, fcntl.LOCK_UN)
        self._lock.close()
        return False


def record_session(job, entry):
    with Sessions() as ss:
        ss.records[job] = {"wake": entry["id"], "note": entry.get("note", ""), "kind": entry.get("kind", ""),
                           "fired": datetime.now().strftime(TIME_FMT), "state": "running"}


def claude_bin():
    """The harness that started the sessions: the session command's program (`claude` by default). A malformed
    setting is the session command's problem, said when a wake fires; here it's "" (the reaper can't look)."""
    try:
        argv = argv_setting("WAKE_SESSION_COMMAND", SESSION_DEFAULT)
    except SystemExit:
        return ""
    return argv[0] if argv else ""


_BLIND = []   # the service's last word on why it couldn't look, so it's said once, not every 2 minutes


def say_blind(why):
    if why != (_BLIND[0] if _BLIND else None):
        _BLIND[:] = [why] if why else []
        if why:
            log("reap-blind", f"can't look at the sessions it started: {why}; trying again every {REAP_CHECK}s")


def background_sessions():
    """`claude agents --json`: {id: entry} for the background sessions it lists, or None when it can't be asked."""
    cmd = [claude_bin(), "agents", "--json"]
    if not cmd[0]:
        say_blind("WAKE_SESSION_COMMAND doesn't parse")
        return None
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
        rows = json.loads(r.stdout) if r.returncode == 0 else None
        why = "" if r.returncode == 0 else f"`{' '.join(cmd)}` rc={r.returncode} {(r.stderr or '').strip()[:120]}"
    except (OSError, ValueError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as e:
        rows, why = None, f"`{' '.join(cmd)}`: {str(e)[:120]}"
    if not isinstance(rows, list):
        say_blind(why or f"`{' '.join(cmd)}` didn't answer a JSON list")
        return None
    say_blind("")
    return {str(a["id"]): a for a in rows if isinstance(a, dict) and a.get("id") and a.get("kind") == "background"}


def waiting_on_permission(a):
    """`claude agents --json` says it's waiting, on a permission prompt (a row without a status counts)."""
    return a.get("status") in (None, "waiting") and "permission" in str(a.get("waitingFor") or "").lower()


def transcript_of(session_id):
    """The session's transcript: <config dir>/projects/<project>/<sessionId>.jsonl, or None."""
    if not session_id or not re.fullmatch(r"[0-9A-Za-z-]{8,64}", str(session_id)):
        return None
    base = Path(os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR") or HOME / ".claude") / "projects"
    found = sorted(base.glob(f"*/{session_id}.jsonl"), key=lambda f: f.stat().st_mtime, reverse=True)
    return found[0] if found else None


TRANSCRIPT_TAIL = 4 * 1024 * 1024   # bytes read from a transcript's end


def last_tool_use(path, tail=TRANSCRIPT_TAIL):
    """(tool, what) for the transcript's last tool call: what it was waiting on. ("", "") when there is none."""
    try:
        with open(path, "rb") as f:
            f.seek(0, os.SEEK_END)
            f.seek(max(0, f.tell() - tail))
            lines = f.read().decode("utf-8", "replace").splitlines()
    except OSError:
        return "", ""
    for line in reversed(lines):
        try:
            d = json.loads(line)
        except ValueError:
            continue
        if not isinstance(d, dict) or d.get("type") != "assistant" or not isinstance(d.get("message"), dict):
            continue
        content = d["message"].get("content")
        if not isinstance(content, list):
            continue
        for block in reversed(content):
            if isinstance(block, dict) and block.get("type") == "tool_use":
                inp = block.get("input") or {}
                what = inp.get("command") if isinstance(inp, dict) and isinstance(inp.get("command"), str) else json.dumps(inp)
                return str(block.get("name") or "a tool"), what
    return "", ""


def task_comment(task, text):
    """WAKE_TASK_COMMENT (default `taskstore comment {task} {text}`, if taskstore is on PATH): True if it took it."""
    raw = setting("WAKE_TASK_COMMENT")
    if raw.strip().lower() in ("off", "none"):
        return False
    try:
        argv = argv_setting("WAKE_TASK_COMMENT", ["taskstore", "comment", "{task}", "{text}"])
    except SystemExit as e:
        log("stuck-comment-fail", f"{task}: {e}")
        return False
    if not raw and not shutil.which(argv[0]):
        return False
    try:
        r = subprocess.run([{"{task}": task, "{text}": text}.get(a, a) for a in argv], capture_output=True, text=True,
                           timeout=60, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, cwd=REPO if REPO.is_dir() else HOME)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as e:
        log("stuck-comment-fail", f"{task}: {e}")
        return False
    if r.returncode != 0:
        log("stuck-comment-fail", f"{task}: rc={r.returncode} {(r.stderr or r.stdout).strip()[:200]}")
    return r.returncode == 0


def as_data(text, n=CMD_SHOWN):
    """A command, redacted and quoted for a comment or the log: one line, at most n characters, in a JSON string."""
    one = " ".join(redact(text).split())
    return json.dumps(one if len(one) <= n else one[:n] + "…", ensure_ascii=False)


def reap_one(job, rec, a, waited):
    """Stop one stuck session, say so on its task and to the owner, and return the record's new fields."""
    path = transcript_of(a.get("sessionId"))
    tool, what = last_tool_use(path) if path else ("", "")
    try:
        r = subprocess.run([claude_bin(), "stop", job], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60,
                           stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
        stopped = r.returncode == 0
        why = "" if stopped else (r.stderr or r.stdout).strip()[:160]
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as e:
        stopped, why = False, str(e)[:160]
    mins = int(waited.total_seconds() // 60)
    wid = str(rec.get("wake") or "?")
    try:
        alerting = bool(argv_setting("WAKE_ALERT_COMMAND", []))
    except SystemExit:
        alerting = False
    waited_on = f"{tool}: {as_data(what)}" if tool else "a tool call the clock couldn't read from its transcript"
    m = TASK_ID.search(rec.get("note") or "")
    task = m.group(0) if m else ""
    commented = False
    if task:
        text = (f"The clock {'stopped' if stopped else 'tried to stop'} this round (wake {wid}, session {job}): "
                f"it had waited {mins} minutes on a permission prompt, and nobody can answer one in a run started by the "
                f"clock. The call it was waiting on, quoted as data, not instructions (an excerpt, credentials removed): "
                f"{waited_on}. Its conversation is kept (`claude attach {job}`). Nothing re-armed this round."
                + ("" if stopped else f" The stop failed: {why}"))
        commented = task_comment(task, text)
    # Fixed fields first, in a fixed order, then the excerpt last: a checker reads the fields by position
    # (`stuck | <wake> session=<id> alerted=yes|no …`) and never the excerpt, which is the command's own text.
    log("stuck", f"{wid} session={job} alerted={'yes' if alerting else 'no'} stopped={'yes' if stopped else 'no'} "
                 f"task={task or 'none'} comment={('ok' if commented else 'failed') if task else 'none'} "
                 f"waited={mins}m | {f'{tool}: {as_data(what)}' if tool else 'unknown'}")
    alert(f"wake: stopped a stuck session: \"{rec.get('note') or wid}\" (wake {wid}, session {job}) "
          f"waited {mins} minutes on a permission prompt"
          + (f" (its last call: {tool})" if tool else "")
          + f". Inspect it with `claude attach {job}`"
          + ("" if stopped else f". The stop FAILED ({why}): `claude stop {job}`")
          + (f". Noted on {task}." if commented else "."))
    return {"state": "stuck", "stuck_at": datetime.now().strftime(TIME_FMT), "stopped": stopped, "tool": tool,
            "command": as_data(what), "task": task, "commented": commented}


def reap_stuck(now=None):
    """One look at the sessions this clock started: stop any that has waited on a permission prompt too long."""
    after = stuck_after()
    if after is None:
        return   # WAKE_STUCK_AFTER=off: not even a look
    with Sessions() as ss:
        records = {k: dict(v) for k, v in ss.records.items() if isinstance(v, dict)}
    if not records:
        return
    agents = background_sessions()
    if agents is None:
        return  # can't ask: look again next time, never guess
    now = now or datetime.now()
    # seen: for each recorded session this look found listed and running, when it started waiting on a permission
    # prompt (None: it isn't waiting). A record not in `seen` wasn't listed, or isn't running.
    seen, reaped = {}, {}
    for job, rec in records.items():
        a = agents.get(job)
        if rec.get("state") != "running" or a is None:
            continue
        if not waiting_on_permission(a):
            seen[job] = None
            continue
        first = rec.get("waiting_since") or now.strftime(TIME_FMT)
        seen[job] = first
        waited = now - datetime.strptime(first, TIME_FMT)
        if after is not None and waited >= after:
            reaped[job] = reap_one(job, rec, a, waited)
    with Sessions() as ss:
        for job, rec in list(ss.records.items()):
            if not isinstance(rec, dict):
                ss.records.pop(job)
                continue
            if job in reaped:
                rec.update(reaped[job])
                rec.pop("waiting_since", None)
            elif job in seen:
                if seen[job]:
                    rec["waiting_since"] = seen[job]
                else:
                    rec.pop("waiting_since", None)
            elif rec.get("state") == "running" and job in records and job not in agents and listed_long(rec, now):
                rec["state"] = "gone"   # it ended (or was stopped by hand): nothing to watch
                rec.pop("waiting_since", None)
            try:
                old = now - datetime.strptime(rec.get("stuck_at") or rec.get("fired") or "", TIME_FMT) > SESSIONS_KEEP
            except (ValueError, TypeError):
                old = True
            if old:
                ss.records.pop(job)


GONE_GRACE = timedelta(minutes=5)   # a session just started may not be listed yet


def listed_long(rec, now):
    """True once a record is old enough that `claude agents` not listing it means it ended."""
    try:
        return now - datetime.strptime(rec.get("fired") or "", TIME_FMT) >= GONE_GRACE
    except (ValueError, TypeError):
        return True


def cmd_reap(_args):
    """(service) One look at this clock's sessions now; the service does it every REAP_CHECK seconds."""
    reap_stuck()


def lane_file(path):
    """The resolved path if it's a .md lane file under one of the repo's lane directories, else None."""
    pf = Path(path)
    pf = (pf if pf.is_absolute() else REPO / pf).resolve()
    if pf.suffix == ".md" and any(pf.is_relative_to(r.resolve()) for r in PROMPT_ROOTS):
        return pf
    return None


def api_answer(request, run):
    """loom's piece API: {caller, path, body:{argv}} -> {status, body}."""
    def refuse(status, error):
        return {"status": status, "body": {"error": error}}
    if not isinstance(request, dict):
        return refuse(400, "not a piece API request")
    caller = request.get("caller") or {}
    agents = [a.strip() for a in setting("WAKE_AGENTS", LOCAL_AGENT).split(",") if a.strip()]
    if caller.get("kind") == "owner":
        pass
    elif caller.get("kind") == "agent" and caller.get("agent") in agents:
        pass
    else:
        return refuse(403, "only the owner and this clock's agents set wakes here")
    if request.get("path") != "run":
        return refuse(404, "the one call is run")
    argv = (request.get("body") or {}).get("argv")
    if not isinstance(argv, list) or not 1 <= len(argv) <= 32 or \
            not all(isinstance(a, str) and len(a) <= 64 * 1024 and "\0" not in a for a in argv):
        return refuse(400, "argv is a list of 1 to 32 plain strings")
    # Whose clock: an agent's own, always; the owner may name any agent's.
    if caller.get("kind") == "agent":
        if "--agent" in argv or any(a.startswith("--agent=") for a in argv):
            return refuse(403, "an agent's own clock is the one its token names")
        agent = caller["agent"]
    else:
        own = owned_by(caller)
        agent = own[0] if own else LOCAL_AGENT
        if argv[0] == "--agent" and len(argv) > 2:
            agent, argv = argv[1], argv[2:]
        if not AGENT_NAME.match(agent):
            return refuse(400, "no agent by that name")
        # An agent owner names only their agents' clocks, and the household's lanes aren't theirs.
        if own is not None and (agent not in own or argv[0] == "lane"):
            return refuse(403, "that's not one of your agents' clocks")
    if argv[0] not in REMOTE_VERBS:
        return refuse(403, f"{argv[0]} runs only on loom's machine; through the API: {', '.join(sorted(REMOTE_VERBS))}")
    # An agent's wake is marked as its own: its -f is held to lane files
    # (checked in cmd_set, on argparse's own reading of the argv), and it
    # only ever fires into a house, never as a session on loom's machine.
    origin = f"agent:{caller['agent']}" if caller.get("kind") == "agent" else ""
    code, out, err = run(argv, origin, agent)
    return {"status": 200, "body": {"exit": code, "stdout": out, "stderr": err[-16384:]}}


def cmd_api(_args):
    try:
        request = json.loads(sys.stdin.read())
    except ValueError:
        request = None

    # The house wrapper appends `--principal <statement>` to every clock call from a body that has one (`wake list` too):
    # taken off here, at the door, before anything reads the argv, and handed to the run on its own, to verify.
    statement = ""
    body = request.get("body") if isinstance(request, dict) else None
    if isinstance(body, dict) and isinstance(body.get("argv"), list) and all(isinstance(a, str) for a in body["argv"]):
        body["argv"], statement = split_principal(body["argv"])
        if len(statement) > 64 * 1024 or "\0" in statement:
            statement = ""

    def run(argv, origin, agent):
        env = {**os.environ, "WAKE_ORIGIN": origin, "WAKE_CALLER": json.dumps(request.get("caller") or {}) if isinstance(request, dict) else "",
               "WAKE_PRINCIPAL_STATEMENT": statement}
        r = subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(SELF), "--agent", agent, *argv], capture_output=True, text=True,
                           cwd=REPO if REPO.is_dir() else HOME, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, timeout=12, env=env)
        return r.returncode, r.stdout, r.stderr
    print(json.dumps(api_answer(request, run)))


def read_spool():
    """The spool as it stands, without the lock (a page reads; it never writes)."""
    try:
        return [json.loads(l) for l in SPOOL.read_text().splitlines() if l.strip()]
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return []


def clock_time(dt):
    return dt.strftime("%I:%M %p").lstrip("0")


def when_text(sc):
    """A schedule's times the way the page says them: 'Weekdays 9:30 AM', 'Sun 6:00 PM', '3:13 AM daily'."""
    times = [sc["at"]] if isinstance(sc["at"], str) else sc["at"]
    times = [t.strip() for x in times for t in str(x).split(",") if t.strip()]
    try:
        at = ", ".join(clock_time(datetime.strptime(t, "%H:%M")) for t in times)
    except ValueError:
        at = ", ".join(times)
    days = (sc.get("days") or "").lower()
    named = {"": None, "mon-fri": "Weekdays", "sat,sun": "Weekends", "sat-sun": "Weekends"}
    if days in named:
        return f"{named[days]} {at}" if named[days] else f"{at} daily"
    return f"{', '.join(d.capitalize() for d in days.split(','))} {at}"


def and_list(words):
    words = list(words)
    return words[0] if len(words) == 1 else ", ".join(words[:-1]) + " and " + words[-1]


def days_spec(value, chips=False):
    """What the page posts for a schedule's days -> how the clock keeps them: '' (every day), 'mon-fri', 'sat,sun',
    or a list ('mon,wed,fri'). It takes the day chips (ticked days, comma-joined) and the old forms alike
    ('mon-fri', 'sat,sun', '' for daily). With `chips`, no day ticked is a mistake, not 'every day'.
    Raises ValueError for anything else."""
    value = "".join(str(value or "").lower().split())
    if not value:
        if chips:
            raise ValueError("Pick at least one day.")
        return ""
    days = days_of(value)   # ValueError on a day it doesn't know
    if days == set(range(7)):
        return ""
    if days == set(range(5)):
        return "mon-fri"
    if days == {5, 6}:
        return "sat,sun"
    return ",".join(DAYS[d] for d in sorted(days))


def days_chips(spec):
    """A schedule's days as the chips field's value: every ticked day, comma-joined ('' is every day: all seven)."""
    try:
        return ",".join(DAYS[d] for d in sorted(days_of((spec or "").lower())))
    except ValueError:
        return ""


def days_field(spec, name="days", label="Days"):
    """The days a schedule runs, as a row of chips (Mon…Sun). Its sheet posts a hidden days_chips=1 with it, so
    no day ticked is refused rather than read as every day."""
    return {"name": name, "label": label, "kind": "checks", "value": days_chips(spec),
            "options": [{"value": d, "label": d.capitalize()} for d in DAYS]}


def when_words(sc):
    """A schedule's times as the row says them: '5:17 AM, every day', '9:30 AM, weekdays', '6:00 PM, Sundays',
    '7:17 AM and 7:17 PM, Mon, Wed and Fri'."""
    times = [sc.get("at")] if isinstance(sc.get("at"), str) else (sc.get("at") or [])
    times = [t.strip() for x in times for t in str(x).split(",") if t.strip()]
    try:
        at = and_list([clock_time(datetime.strptime(t, "%H:%M")) for t in times]) if times else "No time"
    except ValueError:
        at = ", ".join(times)
    try:
        days = days_of((sc.get("days") or "").lower())
    except ValueError:
        return f"{at}, {sc.get('days')}"
    full = ["Mondays", "Tuesdays", "Wednesdays", "Thursdays", "Fridays", "Saturdays", "Sundays"]
    if days == set(range(7)):
        on = "every day"
    elif days == set(range(5)):
        on = "weekdays"
    elif days == {5, 6}:
        on = "weekends"
    elif len(days) == 1:
        on = full[next(iter(days))]
    else:
        on = and_list([DAYS[d].capitalize() for d in sorted(days)])
    return f"{at}, {on}"


WAKE_KINDS = (
    (re.compile(r"\bnudge-watch\b", re.I), "Checking a pull request is moving"),
    (re.compile(r"\breview-watch\b", re.I), "Watching for a review"),
    (re.compile(r"\bci-watch\b", re.I), "Watching a pull request's checks"),
    (re.compile(r"\bdead-?man\b", re.I), "Safety wake, in case nothing else wakes it"),
)


def wake_words(text):
    """What a wake is for, in words, and the ids its note carried: (words, refs).
    't-1652 PR38 nudge-watch round 22' -> ('Checking a pull request is moving, round 22', ['t-1652', 'PR 38']).
    The ids go to the wake's detail (and quietly into a row's meta); a note with no pattern it knows reads as
    written, less the task ids it leads with and any wake id."""
    text = " ".join(str(text or "").split())
    refs = []
    m = re.match(r"((?:t-\d+)(?:\s*/\s*t-\d+)*)\s*[:\-–—]?\s+", text)
    if m:
        refs += re.findall(r"t-\d+", m.group(1))
        text = text[m.end():]
    prs = re.findall(r"\bPR\s?#?(\d+)\b", text)
    refs += [f"PR {n}" for n in prs]
    rnd = re.search(r"\bround (\d+)\b", text)
    for pat, words in WAKE_KINDS:
        if pat.search(text):
            for t in re.findall(r"\bt-\d+\b", text):
                if t not in refs:
                    refs.append(t)
            refs += [w for w in re.findall(r"\bw-[0-9a-f]{6}\b", text) if w not in refs]
            return words + (f", round {rnd.group(1)}" if rnd else ""), refs
    text = re.sub(r"\bPR\s?#?\d+\b\s*", "", text)
    wids = re.findall(r"\bw-[0-9a-f]{6}\b", text)
    refs += wids
    text = re.sub(r"(?:,?\s+(?:after|from|of|for))?\s*\bw-[0-9a-f]{6}\b", "", text).strip(" ,:;")
    text = " ".join(text.split())
    return (text[:1].upper() + text[1:]) if text else "", refs


def day_time(dt, now):
    """'9:30 AM', 'Tomorrow 3:13 AM', 'Yesterday 9:00 PM', 'Sun 6:00 PM', 'Oct 3, 9:30 AM'."""
    days = (dt.date() - now.date()).days
    t = clock_time(dt)
    if days == 0:
        return t
    if days in (1, -1):
        return f"{'Tomorrow' if days == 1 else 'Yesterday'} {t}"
    if -6 <= days <= 6:
        return f"{dt.strftime('%a')} {t}"
    return f"{dt.strftime('%b')} {dt.day}, {t}"


def until_text(dt, now):
    mins = round((dt - now).total_seconds() / 60)
    if mins <= 1:
        return "within a minute"
    if mins < 60:
        return f"in {mins} minutes"
    hours = round(mins / 60)
    if hours < 48:
        return f"in {hours} hour{'s' if hours != 1 else ''}"
    return f"in {round(hours / 24)} days"


# How much of the next wake's words the tile carries: loom's app wraps a tile's line to three lines (it cut it at one
# before, and this was 40 so the cut came here, mid-word: "Art: Checking a pull request is moving, roun…").
TILE_BRIEF = 120


def short(text, n=80):
    text = " ".join(str(text).split())
    return text if len(text) <= n else text[: n - 1] + "…"


def pretty(name):
    return name.replace("-", " ").capitalize()


def what_of(e):
    """What a wake is, for a label. A schedule occurrence's note is the piece's own ("schedule planning-prepare: ...")
    and reads as words ("Planning prepare (schedule): ..."); any other note is shown as written; a lane file by its name in words."""
    note, sname = e.get("note") or "", e.get("schedule")
    if sname:
        head = f"schedule {sname}"
        own = note[len(head):].removeprefix(":").strip() if note.startswith(head) else note
        return f"{pretty(sname)} (schedule)" + (f": {own}" if own else "")
    if note:
        return note
    if e.get("prompt_file") or e.get("lane"):
        return pretty(Path(e.get("prompt_file") or e["lane"]).stem)
    return e.get("prompt", "")


def next_at(dt, now):
    """'Next at 8:50 AM', 'Next tomorrow at 3:13 AM', 'Next Sun 6:00 PM'."""
    s = day_time(dt, now)
    if s[0].isdigit():
        return f"Next at {s}"
    return "Next " + s.replace("Tomorrow ", "tomorrow at ").replace("Yesterday ", "yesterday at ")


FIRE_EVENTS = ("fire", "fire-fail", "fire-giveup", "fire-held", "fire-refused")


def recent_fires(lines, n=8):
    """The last n fires from the clock's log: (when, id, event, what it was, detail)."""
    names, out = {}, []
    wid = re.compile(r"\b(w-[0-9a-f]{6})\b")
    for line in lines:
        parts = line.split(" | ", 2)
        if len(parts) < 3:
            continue
        stamp, event, detail = parts
        m = wid.search(detail)
        if event == "set" and m:
            note = re.search(r"note='(.*)'$", detail) or re.search(r'note="(.*)"$', detail)
            names[m.group(1)] = note.group(1) if note and note.group(1) else ""
        elif event in ("schedule-next", "schedule-set", "schedule-skip") and m:
            names[wid.findall(detail)[-1]] = pretty(detail.split(":", 1)[0])
        elif event == "deadman" and m:
            names[m.group(1)] = "Dead-man wake"
        elif event == "fire-fail" and m:
            # its retry carries the same wake under a new id
            ids = wid.findall(detail)
            if len(ids) > 1:
                names[ids[-1]] = names.get(ids[0], "")
        if event in FIRE_EVENTS and m:
            try:
                when = datetime.strptime(stamp, TIME_FMT)
            except ValueError:
                continue
            out.append((when, m.group(1), event, names.get(m.group(1), ""), detail))
    return out[-n:]


def time_field(name, label, value):
    """A form's time of day: loom's `time` field (the device's own picker, 12-hour where that's how its owner reads
    time), several allowed. loom refuses a page whose time field isn't strictly
    HH:MM, so a stored "5:17" is sent as "05:17"; anything it can't read falls back to the text box it used to be."""
    times = [t.strip() for t in str(value or "").split(",") if t.strip()]
    norm = []
    for t in times:
        m = re.fullmatch(r"(\d{1,2}):(\d{2})", t)
        if not m or int(m.group(1)) > 23 or int(m.group(2)) > 59:
            return {"name": name, "label": label, "kind": "text", "required": True, "value": ",".join(times),
                    "hint": "24-hour time, like 09:30 or 19:17; several, comma separated"}
        norm.append(f"{int(m.group(1)):02d}:{m.group(2)}")
    f = {"name": name, "label": label, "kind": "time", "multiple": True, "required": True,
         "hint": "Add another time if it runs more than once a day."}
    if norm:
        f["value"] = ",".join(norm)
    return f


def ui_view():
    """Every agent's clock: {agent, schedules, entries, recent, paused}. LOOM_SCOPE narrows it to one."""
    scope = os.environ.get("LOOM_SCOPE", "").strip()
    agents = clock_agents()
    if scope:
        agents = ([a for a in agents if a == scope] or [scope]) if AGENT_NAME.match(scope) else []
    out = []
    for agent in agents:
        configure(agent)
        try:
            tail = LOG.read_text().splitlines()[-3000:]
        except OSError:
            tail = []
        out.append({"agent": agent, "schedules": load_schedules(), "entries": sorted(read_spool(), key=lambda e: e["at"]),
                    "recent": recent_fires(tail), "paused": paused()})
    configure(LOCAL_AGENT)
    return out


def name_of(agent):
    """An agent's name as people say it: its id, capitalized."""
    return str(agent).capitalize()


def brief_of(e):
    """What a wake is, in a few words, for the tile and an agent's card: a schedule occurrence by its schedule's name
    alone ("Planning retro"), any other in words without its ids; the Clock's own page keeps the rest of its note."""
    return pretty(e["schedule"]) if e.get("schedule") else (wake_words(what_of(e))[0] or what_of(e))


def upcoming(entries):
    """The wakes an agent has coming: not the clock's own house checks ("Checking that its house started")."""
    return [e for e in entries if e.get("kind") != "watch"]


def ui_manifest(view, now=None):
    now = now or datetime.now()
    scheds = sum(len(v["schedules"]) for v in view)
    nxt = min(((v, e) for v in view for e in upcoming(v["entries"])), key=lambda ve: ve[1]["at"], default=None)
    stopped = [name_of(v["agent"]) for v in view if v["paused"]]
    if stopped:
        value, detail, tone = "Paused", f"{', '.join(stopped)}: wakes held", "warn"
    elif nxt:
        at = datetime.strptime(nxt[1]["at"], TIME_FMT)
        value = day_time(at, now)
        # Up to three lines on a phone's tile (loom wraps a tile's line there); the agent's clock, a tap away, has the rest.
        detail, tone = f"{name_of(nxt[0]['agent'])}: {short(brief_of(nxt[1]), TILE_BRIEF)}", None
    else:
        value, detail, tone = "Nothing", "nothing pending", "warn"
    # The tile opens the clock it's about: that agent's own (the household's Clock is only loom's lanes).
    tile = {"label": "Clock", "value": value, "detail": detail,
            "page": f"agent:{(nxt[0]['agent'] if nxt else view[0]['agent'])}" if view else ""}
    if tone:
        tile["tone"] = tone
    # owners: 2 (loom docs/specs/owners.md): an agent owner sees and sets only their agents' clocks.
    # Loom's own lanes on the household's Clock, under Setup (rarely visited); each agent's on its own pages.
    return {"v": 2, "tab": {"label": "Clock", "kind": "setting"}, "agentTab": {"label": "Clock"}, "scope": True, "owners": 2,
            "tile": tile, "asks": [], "agents": agent_reports(view, now),
            "notices": []}


def agent_reports(view, now):
    """Each agent's Next, for its card on loom's Home (loom's docs/extensions.md, "agents"): its next
    wake and what it's for. A paused clock is unavailable: its wakes are held until it resumes."""
    out = {}
    for v in view:
        nxt = next((e for e in upcoming(v["entries"]) if not e.get("held")), None)
        held = sum(1 for e in v["entries"] if e.get("held"))
        if v["paused"]:
            out[v["agent"]] = {"state": "unavailable", "reason": f"its clock is paused" + (f" ({held} wake{'s' if held != 1 else ''} held)" if held else ""),
                               "readings": [{"label": "Next", "value": "paused", "tone": "warn", "page": ""}]}
        elif nxt:
            at = datetime.strptime(nxt["at"], TIME_FMT)
            out[v["agent"]] = {"readings": [{"label": "Next", "value": f"{short(brief_of(nxt), 40)}, {day_time(at, now)}", "detail": until_text(at, now), "page": ""}]}
        else:
            out[v["agent"]] = {"readings": [{"label": "Next", "value": "nothing pending", "tone": "warn", "page": ""}]}
    return out


def lanes():
    """The local agent's lane files, for the page's picker: the first lane directory's .md files."""
    return sorted(p.relative_to(REPO).as_posix() for p in (REPO / lane_dir()).glob("*.md"))


def until_words(dt, now):
    """'at 10:05 AM', 'tomorrow at 3:13 AM', 'on Sun 6:00 PM': the tail of 'Art wakes …'."""
    s = next_at(dt, now).removeprefix("Next ")
    return s if s.startswith(("at ", "tomorrow", "yesterday")) else "on " + s


def hero(c, now):
    """The clock's top: a headline that says when the agent wakes next, and the clock's switch, with Wake now."""
    agent, name = c["agent"], name_of(c["agent"])
    nxt = next((e for e in upcoming(c["entries"]) if not e.get("held")), None)
    held = sum(1 for e in c["entries"] if e.get("held"))
    switch = {"label": "Clock", "toggle": {"action": "clock", "on": not c["paused"], "fields": {"agent": agent}}}
    if c["paused"]:
        since = datetime.strptime(c["paused"]["since"], TIME_FMT)
        head = {"type": "health", "tone": "warn", "text": f"{name}'s clock is paused",
                "detail": f"Since {day_time(since, now)}. " + (f"{held} wake{'s' if held != 1 else ''} held: each fires once when it runs again."
                                                               if held else "Wakes that come due are held, not lost.")}
        switch.update(value="Paused", tone="warn", detail="Turn it on and each held wake fires once.")
    elif nxt:
        at = datetime.strptime(nxt["at"], TIME_FMT)
        words = wake_words(what_of(nxt))[0] or "A wake"
        head = {"type": "health", "tone": "ok", "text": f"{name} wakes {until_words(at, now)}",
                "detail": f"{until_text(at, now)[:1].upper()}{until_text(at, now)[1:]}: {words}."}
        switch.update(value="Running", detail="Turned off, wakes that come due are held, not lost.")
    else:
        head = {"type": "health", "tone": "warn", "text": "Nothing pending", "detail": f"{name} has no wake coming."}
        switch.update(value="Running", detail="Turned off, wakes that come due are held, not lost.")
    return [head, {"type": "panel", "rows": [switch],
                   "action": {"action": "now", "label": "Wake now", "tone": "primary", "fields": {"agent": agent}}}]


def lane_note(note):
    """A schedule's note without the piece's own 'loom lane: ' at its head."""
    note = note or ""
    return note.removeprefix("loom lane").removeprefix(":").strip()


def schedule_blocks(c, now):
    """An agent's schedules as rows: name, when in words, next and what it's for; Add a schedule last."""
    agent = c["agent"]
    nxt = {e["schedule"]: e["at"] for e in c["entries"] if e.get("schedule")}
    rows = []
    for name, sc in sorted(c["schedules"].items(), key=lambda kv: nxt.get(kv[0], "9")):
        at = nxt.get(name)
        note = lane_note(sc.get("note")) if sc.get("loom_lane") else (sc.get("note") or "")
        detail = (next_at(datetime.strptime(at, TIME_FMT), now) if at else "None armed") \
            + (" · a loom lane" if sc.get("loom_lane") else "") + (f" · {note}" if note else "")
        rows.append({"label": pretty(name), "value": when_words(sc), "detail": detail, "page": f"schedule/{agent}/{name}"})
    lane_opts = [{"value": l, "label": pretty(Path(l).stem)} for l in lanes()][:50]
    rows.append({"label": "Add a schedule", "value": "A wake that comes back on the days and times you pick", "edit": {
        "action": "schedule-set", "title": "New schedule", "submit": "Add", "hidden": {"agent": agent, "days_chips": "1"},
        "note": "A recurring wake keeps one run pending and arms the next when it fires.",
        "fields": [
            {"name": "name", "label": "Name", "kind": "text", "required": True, "hint": "lowercase and dashes, like nightly"},
            time_field("at", "Time", ""),
            days_field(""),
            {"name": "lane", "label": "Lane", "kind": "choice", "required": True, "options": lane_opts}
            if agent == LOCAL_AGENT else
            {"name": "lane", "label": "Lane", "kind": "text", "required": True, "hint": "a file in its repo, like routines/x.md"},
            {"name": "note", "label": "What it's for", "kind": "text"},
        ]}})
    blocks = [] if c["schedules"] else [{"type": "text", "text": "No schedules yet.", "tone": "muted"}]
    return blocks + [{"type": "panel", "rows": rows}]


def wake_row(e, agent, now):
    """A pending wake as a list row: what it's for in words; its time, and quietly the task it's for. Its ids are on its page."""
    words, refs = wake_words(what_of(e))
    meta = [day_time(datetime.strptime(e["at"], TIME_FMT), now)]
    if e.get("held"):
        meta.append("held")
    if e.get("fails"):
        meta.append(f"retry {e['fails']}")
    tasks = [r for r in refs if r.startswith("t-")]
    if tasks:
        meta.append(", ".join(tasks[:3]))
    row = {"text": words or "A wake", "meta": " · ".join(meta), "page": f"wake/{agent}/{e['id']}"}
    if e.get("held"):
        row["tone"] = "warn"
    elif e.get("fails"):
        row["tone"] = "bad"
    return row


def oneoff_blocks(c, now):
    agent = c["agent"]
    rows = [e for e in c["entries"] if e["kind"] != "schedule"]
    wakes = sum(1 for e in rows if e["kind"] == "wake")
    items = [wake_row(e, agent, now) for e in rows[:100]]
    return [{"type": "text", "text": f"{wakes} one-off wake{'s' if wakes != 1 else ''} pending, of {MAX_PENDING} at most. "
                                     "The safety wake comes when nothing else is.", "tone": "muted"},
            {"type": "list", "items": items} if items else {"type": "text", "text": "None pending.", "tone": "muted"}]


def recent_blocks(c, now):
    items = []
    for when, wid, event, what, detail in reversed(c["recent"]):
        bad = event in ("fire-fail", "fire-giveup", "fire-refused")
        why = {"fire-fail": "failed, retrying", "fire-giveup": "failed, gave up", "fire-refused": "refused",
               "fire-held": "held (paused)"}.get(event)
        house = re.search(r"\b(h-\d+)\b", detail)
        words, refs = wake_words(what)
        tasks = [r for r in refs if r.startswith("t-")]
        meta = day_time(when, now) + (f" · {why}" if why else "") + (" · in a house" if house and not bad else "") \
            + (f" · {', '.join(tasks[:3])}" if tasks else "")
        items.append({"text": words or "A wake", "meta": meta, "tone": "bad" if bad else ("warn" if event == "fire-held" else "ok")})
    return [{"type": "list", "items": items}] if items else [{"type": "text", "text": "No wakes yet.", "tone": "muted"}]


def ui_page(view, path, now=None, lanes=True, scope=None):
    """The clock's pages. With `scope` (an agent's own Clock tab, LOOM_SCOPE): that agent's next wake,
    schedule, recent and one-off wakes. Without (the household's Clock, under Setup): loom's own lanes and
    a link to each agent's clock. Most of what a clock shows is one agent's, so it lives on that agent's
    pages; the household's page is only what's the household's."""
    now = now or datetime.now()
    path = path or ""
    m = re.fullmatch(r"schedule/([a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,39})/([a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,39})", path)
    if m:
        return schedule_page(view, m.group(1), m.group(2), now, lanes=lanes)
    m = re.fullmatch(r"lane/([a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,39})", path)
    if m:
        return lane_page(m.group(1), view, now)
    m = re.fullmatch(r"wake/([a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,39})/(w-[0-9a-f]{6})", path)
    if m:
        return wake_page(view, m.group(1), m.group(2), now)
    if path:
        return {"title": "Not found", "sections": []}
    if not scope:
        return household_clock_page(view, now, lanes)
    view = [c for c in view if c["agent"] == scope]
    many = len(view) > 1
    sections = []
    for c in view[:3]:
        who = f"{name_of(c['agent'])} · " if many else ""
        sections.append({"id": f"next-{c['agent']}", "title": f"{name_of(c['agent'])}" if many else "", "blocks": hero(c, now)})
        sections.append({"id": f"schedule-{c['agent']}", "title": f"{who}Schedules", "blocks": schedule_blocks(c, now)})
        sections.append({"id": f"oneoff-{c['agent']}", "title": f"{who}Coming up", "side": True, "blocks": oneoff_blocks(c, now)})
        sections.append({"id": f"recent-{c['agent']}", "title": f"{who}Recent", "side": True, "blocks": recent_blocks(c, now)})
    if not sections:
        sections.append({"id": "none", "title": "", "blocks": [{"type": "text", "text": "No clock here.", "tone": "muted"}]})
    runs = [{"text": pretty(nm), "meta": when_words(ln) + (" · on loom's machine" if ln.get("local") else ""), "page": f"household:lane/{nm}"}
            for nm, ln in sorted(load_lanes().items()) if ln.get("agent") == scope]
    if lanes and runs:   # the household's lanes are its owners' to see (an agent owner's view has none)
        sections.append({"id": "its-lanes", "title": "Loom lanes it runs", "side": True, "blocks": [
            {"type": "text", "tone": "muted", "text": "The household's work on a schedule, assigned to it. They're set on loom's Clock, under Setup."},
            {"type": "list", "items": runs}]})
    return {"title": "Clock", "intro": "When this agent wakes: its schedules, and the one-off wakes it set itself.", "sections": sections[:10]}


def household_clock_page(view, now, lanes=True):
    """Loom's own Clock: the household's lanes, and each agent's clock one link away (its own pages)."""
    sections = []
    if lanes:
        sections.append({"id": "loom-lanes", "title": "Loom lanes", "blocks": lane_blocks() + new_lane_blocks()})
    rows = []
    for c in view:
        e = next((e for e in upcoming(c["entries"]) if not e.get("held")), None)
        row = {"label": f"{name_of(c['agent'])}'s clock", "agent": c["agent"], "page": f"agent:{c['agent']}"}
        if c.get("paused"):
            row.update(value="Paused", tone="warn", detail="Its wakes are held until it runs again.")
        elif e:
            row.update(value=next_at(datetime.strptime(e["at"], TIME_FMT), now), detail=brief_of(e) or "A wake")
        else:
            row.update(value="Nothing pending")
        rows.append(row)
    if rows:
        sections.append({"id": "agents", "title": "Each agent's clock", "side": True, "blocks": [
            {"type": "text", "tone": "muted", "text": "Each agent's schedules and wakes are on its own pages."},
            {"type": "panel", "rows": rows}]})
    if not sections:
        sections.append({"id": "none", "title": "", "blocks": [{"type": "text", "text": "No clock here.", "tone": "muted"}]})
    return {"title": "Clock", "intro": "The household's work on a schedule, each lane run by one of its agents.", "sections": sections}


def where_words(ln):
    return "on loom's machine" if ln.get("local") else "in a house"


def lane_blocks():
    """The household's lanes as rows: whose, when and where in a sentence ('Art · 5:17 AM, every day · on loom's machine')."""
    lanes = load_lanes()
    rows = [{"label": pretty(nm), "value": f"{name_of(ln['agent'])} · {when_words(ln)}" + (" · on loom's machine" if ln.get("local") else ""),
             "agent": ln["agent"], "page": f"lane/{nm}", **({"detail": ln["note"]} if ln.get("note") else {})}
            for nm, ln in sorted(lanes.items())]
    if not rows:
        return [{"type": "text", "tone": "muted", "text": "No loom lanes yet."}]
    return [{"type": "panel", "rows": rows}]


def lane_when(ln):
    return when_text(ln)


def agent_field(name, label, value, agents):
    """Whose: side by side when there are a few agents, else a picker."""
    opts = [{"value": a, "label": name_of(a)} for a in agents]
    kind = "segmented" if 2 <= len(opts) <= 5 else "choice"
    return {"name": name, "label": label, "kind": kind, "value": value, "options": opts}


WHERE_OPTIONS = [{"value": "house", "label": "In a house"}, {"value": "local", "label": "On loom's machine"}]


def lane_fields(ln, agents):
    """The settings a new lane's sheet asks for (the lane's own page sets each on its own row)."""
    return [
        agent_field("to", "Whose", ln.get("agent") or (agents[0] if agents else LOCAL_AGENT), agents),
        time_field("at", "When", ln["at"] if isinstance(ln.get("at"), str) else ",".join(ln.get("at") or [])),
        days_field(ln.get("days") or ""),
        {"name": "where", "label": "Where it runs", "kind": "segmented", "value": "local" if ln.get("local") else "house",
         "options": WHERE_OPTIONS, "hint": "On loom's machine is for work that needs it: systemd, files outside the repo."},
        {"name": "note", "label": "What it's for", "kind": "text", "value": ln.get("note") or ""},
    ]


def lane_page(nm, view=(), now=None):
    """A loom lane as a panel: When, Where, Whose, What it's for and its text, each a row that says its value and
    opens one control; Run now at its foot; the text to read; Remove, which asks first."""
    now = now or datetime.now()
    ln = load_lanes().get(nm)
    if not ln:
        return {"title": "Not found", "sections": []}
    agents = household_agents() or clock_agents()
    if ln["agent"] not in agents:
        agents = [ln["agent"], *agents]
    agent, whose = ln["agent"], name_of(ln["agent"])
    key = {"name": nm, "agent": agent}
    text = ln["text"]
    c = find_clock(list(view), agent)
    nxt = next((e["at"] for e in (c["entries"] if c else []) if e.get("schedule") == nm), None)
    at_value = ln["at"] if isinstance(ln.get("at"), str) else ",".join(ln.get("at") or [])
    when = {"label": "When", "value": when_words(ln),
            "edit": {"action": "lane-edit", "title": "When it runs", "submit": "Save", "hidden": {**key, "days_chips": "1"},
                     "fields": [time_field("at", "Time", at_value), days_field(ln.get("days") or "")]}}
    if nxt:
        when["detail"] = next_at(datetime.strptime(nxt, TIME_FMT), now)
    where = {"label": "Where", "value": "On loom's machine" if ln.get("local") else "In a house",
             "detail": "For work that needs it: systemd, files outside the repo." if ln.get("local") else f"{whose}'s house, on any box.",
             "choice": {"action": "lane-edit", "name": "where", "value": "local" if ln.get("local") else "house",
                        "options": WHERE_OPTIONS, "fields": key}}
    who = {"label": "Whose", "value": whose, "agent": agent, "detail": f"Its runs are {whose}'s work, as {whose}."}
    if 2 <= len(agents) <= 5:
        who["choice"] = {"action": "lane-edit", "name": "to", "value": agent,
                         "options": [{"value": a, "label": name_of(a)} for a in agents], "fields": key}
    elif len(agents) > 5:
        who["edit"] = {"action": "lane-edit", "title": "Whose it is", "submit": "Save", "hidden": key,
                       "fields": [agent_field("to", "Whose", agent, agents)]}
    note = {"label": "What it's for", "value": ln.get("note") or "Not said yet",
            "edit": {"action": "lane-edit", "title": "What it's for", "submit": "Save", "hidden": key,
                     "fields": [{"name": "note", "label": "What it's for", "kind": "text", "value": ln.get("note") or "", "required": True}]}}
    if not ln.get("note"):
        note["tone"] = "muted"
    src = repo_relative(ln.get("source") or "")
    words = len(text.split())
    shown = text if len(text) <= 19000 else text[:19000] + "\n\n… (the rest is longer than the page shows; `wake lane text " + nm + "`)"
    readrow = {"label": "What it does", "value": f"{words:,} word{'s' if words != 1 else ''} of instructions",
               "sheet": {"title": "What it does", "blocks": [{"type": "prose", "text": shown}]}}
    if src:
        readrow["detail"] = f"Set from {src}"
    replacerow = {"label": "Replace the text", "value": "Paste a whole new text",
                  "detail": "Or edit its file, then set it again with wake lane set." if src else None,
                  "edit": {"action": "lane-text", "title": "Replace the text", "submit": "Replace", "hidden": key,
                           "note": f"Paste the whole new text: it replaces all {len(text):,} characters.",
                           "fields": [{"name": "text", "label": "The lane's text", "kind": "textarea", "required": True}]}}
    if not src:
        del replacerow["detail"]
    return {"title": pretty(nm), "intro": f"A loom lane: the household's work, run by {whose}.",
            "sections": [
                {"id": "settings", "title": "", "blocks": [
                    {"type": "panel", "rows": [when, where, who, note],
                     "action": {"action": "lane-run", "label": "Run now", "tone": "primary", "fields": key}}]},
                {"id": "text", "title": "Its text", "blocks": [{"type": "panel", "rows": [readrow, replacerow]}]},
                {"id": "remove", "title": "", "side": True, "blocks": [
                    {"type": "buttons", "items": [{"action": "lane-rm", "label": "Remove this lane", "tone": "danger",
                                                   "confirm": f"{whose}'s schedule for it goes, and its text is gone from loom"
                                                              + (f" ({src} stays)." if src else "."),
                                                   "fields": key}]}]},
            ]}


def new_lane_blocks():
    agents = household_agents() or clock_agents()
    return [{"type": "panel", "rows": [{"label": "New loom lane", "value": "Work on a schedule, run by one of the household's agents", "edit": {
        "action": "lane-new", "title": "New loom lane", "submit": "Add", "hidden": {"days_chips": "1"}, "fields": [
            {"name": "name", "label": "Name", "kind": "text", "required": True, "hint": "lowercase and dashes, like directory-upkeep"},
            *lane_fields({}, agents),
            {"name": "text", "label": "What it does", "kind": "textarea", "required": True, "hint": "The lane's prompt, as its house gets it"}]}}]}]


def find_clock(view, agent):
    return next((c for c in view if c["agent"] == agent), None)


def schedule_page(view, agent, name, now, lanes=True):
    """A schedule as a panel: When (its sheet sets the time and days), what it's for, what it runs, whose; Run now."""
    c = find_clock(view, agent)
    sc = c and c["schedules"].get(name)
    if not sc:
        return {"title": "Not found", "sections": []}
    at = next((e["at"] for e in c["entries"] if e.get("schedule") == name), None)
    runs = repo_relative(sc.get("prompt_file") or sc.get("lane") or "")
    at_value = sc["at"] if isinstance(sc["at"], str) else ",".join(sc["at"])
    keep = {"agent": agent, "name": name, "lane": runs, "model": sc.get("model") or DEFAULT_MODEL}
    if sc.get("slot"):
        keep["slot"] = sc["slot"]
    lane = sc.get("loom_lane") and name in load_lanes()
    when = {"label": "When", "value": when_words(sc),
            "detail": next_at(datetime.strptime(at, TIME_FMT), now) if at else "None armed"}
    note_text = lane_note(sc.get("note")) if sc.get("loom_lane") else (sc.get("note") or "")
    note = {"label": "What it's for", "value": note_text or "Not said"}
    if not note_text:
        note["tone"] = "muted"
    if runs:   # a lane file's schedule is set again from here; an inline prompt can't come back through a form
        when["edit"] = {"action": "schedule-set", "title": "When it runs", "submit": "Save",
                        "hidden": {**keep, "note": sc.get("note") or "", "days_chips": "1"},
                        "fields": [time_field("at", "Time", at_value), days_field(sc.get("days") or "")]}
        note["edit"] = {"action": "schedule-set", "title": "What it's for", "submit": "Save",
                        "hidden": {**keep, "at": at_value, "days": sc.get("days") or ""},
                        "fields": [{"name": "note", "label": "What it's for", "kind": "text", "value": sc.get("note") or ""}]}
    elif lane and lanes:
        when.update(page=f"household:lane/{name}", detail=when["detail"] + " · a loom lane: set on loom's Clock")
    body = runs or sc.get("prompt", "")
    what = {"label": "What it runs", "value": pretty(Path(runs).stem) if runs else ("A loom lane's text" if sc.get("loom_lane") else "A prompt of its own"),
            "sheet": {"title": "What it runs", "blocks": [{"type": "code", "label": "Lane file" if runs else "Prompt",
                                                            "text": body if len(body) <= 1900 else body[:1900] + "…"}]}}
    rows = [when, note, what,
            {"label": "Model", "value": sc.get("model", DEFAULT_MODEL)},
            {"label": "Whose", "value": name_of(agent), "agent": agent}]
    sections = [{"id": "schedule", "title": "", "blocks": [
        {"type": "panel", "rows": rows,
         "action": {"action": "run", "label": "Run now", "tone": "primary", "fields": {"agent": agent, "name": name}}}]}]
    if runs:
        sections.append({"id": "remove", "title": "", "side": True, "blocks": [{"type": "buttons", "items": [
            {"action": "schedule-rm", "label": "Remove", "tone": "danger", "fields": {"agent": agent, "name": name},
             "confirm": f"{pretty(name)} stops recurring and its pending run is cancelled."}]}]})
    return {"title": pretty(name), "sections": sections}


WAKE_KIND_WORDS = {"wake": "A one-off wake", "deadman": "The safety wake: it comes when nothing else is pending",
                   "schedule": "One run of a schedule", "watch": "Checking that its house started"}


def wake_page(view, agent, wid, now):
    """A pending wake: what it's for in words, when, what kind; its id, note as written and what it runs behind Details."""
    c = find_clock(view, agent)
    e = c and next((e for e in c["entries"] if e["id"] == wid), None)
    if not e:
        return {"title": "Not found", "sections": [{"id": "gone", "title": "", "blocks": [
            {"type": "text", "text": "That wake isn't pending any more: it fired or was cancelled.", "tone": "muted"}]}]}
    words, refs = wake_words(what_of(e))
    at = datetime.strptime(e["at"], TIME_FMT)
    when = {"label": "When", "value": f"{day_time(at, now)}, {until_text(at, now)}" if at > now else day_time(at, now)}
    if e.get("held"):
        when.update(tone="warn", detail="Held: it fires once the clock runs again.")
    elif e.get("fails"):
        when.update(tone="bad", detail=f"Retry {e['fails']}: its last try failed.")
    kind = WAKE_KIND_WORDS.get(e["kind"], e["kind"])
    if e.get("schedule"):
        kind = f"One run of {pretty(e['schedule'])}"
    rows = [{"label": "What it's for", "value": words or "Not said"}, when, {"label": "What it is", "value": kind},
            {"label": "Set", "value": day_time(datetime.strptime(e["created"], TIME_FMT), now)}]
    tasks = [r for r in refs if r.startswith("t-")]
    prs = [r for r in refs if r.startswith("PR ")]
    if tasks:
        rows.append({"label": "For", "value": ", ".join(f"task {t}" for t in tasks)
                     + (f", {', '.join(prs)}" if prs else "")})
    record = [{"label": "Id", "value": wid}, {"label": "Note, as written", "value": e.get("note") or "(none)"}]
    if e.get("slot"):
        record.append({"label": "House slot", "value": e["slot"]})
    sheet = [{"type": "kv", "items": record}]
    body = e.get("prompt") or repo_relative(e.get("prompt_file") or e.get("lane", ""))
    if body:
        sheet.append({"type": "code", "label": "What it runs", "text": body if len(body) <= 1900 else body[:1900] + "…"})
    rows.append({"label": "Details", "value": "Its id, its note as written, and what it runs", "sheet": {"title": "The wake's record", "blocks": sheet}})
    sections = [{"id": "wake", "title": "", "blocks": [{"type": "panel", "rows": rows}]}]
    if e["kind"] != "deadman":
        sections.append({"id": "cancel", "title": "", "side": True, "blocks": [{"type": "buttons", "items": [
            {"action": "cancel", "label": "Cancel this wake" if e["kind"] == "wake" else "Skip this run", "tone": "danger",
             "fields": {"agent": agent, "id": wid},
             "confirm": "This wake won't fire." if e["kind"] == "wake" else "Skips just this run; the next is armed."}]}]})
    # The header holds a short title; what it's for, which runs long, is the first row and wraps.
    title = {"wake": "One-off wake", "deadman": "Safety wake", "watch": "House check"}.get(e["kind"], "Wake")
    if e.get("schedule"):
        title = pretty(e["schedule"])
    return {"title": title, "sections": sections}


def owned_by(caller):
    """The agents an owner caller owns (loom docs/specs/owners.md): None for a household owner (or no caller), else their list."""
    if not isinstance(caller, dict) or caller.get("kind") != "owner":
        return None
    a = caller.get("agents")
    if a is None or a == "*":
        return None
    return [x for x in a if isinstance(x, str) and AGENT_NAME.match(x)] if isinstance(a, list) else []


def ui_act(req, run):
    """The page's buttons, switches and sheets -> {ok, message, page?, undo?}. `run(agent, argv)` is the CLI."""
    if not isinstance(req, dict):
        return {"ok": False, "message": "Not an action."}
    action, f = req.get("action"), req.get("fields") if isinstance(req.get("fields"), dict) else {}
    own = owned_by(req.get("caller"))
    agent = str(f.get("agent") or (own[0] if own else LOCAL_AGENT))
    if not AGENT_NAME.match(agent):
        return {"ok": False, "message": "No clock by that name."}
    # An agent owner: their agents' clocks only, and the household's lanes are a household owner's.
    if own is not None and (agent not in own or str(action).startswith("lane")):
        return {"ok": False, "message": "That's not one of your agents' clocks; ask a household owner."}
    name = name_of(agent)
    pick = lambda k: str(f.get(k) or "").strip()
    chips = pick("days_chips") == "1"

    def go(argv, message, **extra):
        code, out, err = run(agent, argv)
        if code != 0:
            return {"ok": False, "message": (err.strip().removeprefix("wake: ") or out.strip() or "That didn't work.")[:300]}
        return {"ok": True, "message": message, **extra}

    def days():
        """The posted days as the clock keeps them; ValueError says what's wrong."""
        try:
            return days_spec(f.get("days"), chips=chips)
        except ValueError as e:
            if chips and not pick("days"):
                raise ValueError("Pick at least one day.") from e
            raise ValueError("Days are mon..sun: a list (mon,wed,fri), a range (mon-fri), or none for every day.") from e

    if action in ("lane-new", "lane-edit"):
        nm = pick("name")
        cur = dict(load_lanes().get(nm) or {}) if action == "lane-edit" else {}
        if action == "lane-edit" and not cur:
            return {"ok": False, "message": f"There's no loom lane {nm}."}
        # A sheet or a switch posts only what it sets; the rest of the lane stays as it is.
        argv = ["lane", "set", nm]
        if action == "lane-new" or "to" in f:
            argv += ["--agent", pick("to")]
            cur["agent"] = pick("to")
        if action == "lane-new" or "at" in f:
            argv += ["--at", pick("at").replace(" ", "")]
            cur["at"] = pick("at").replace(" ", "")
        if action == "lane-new" or "days" in f:
            try:
                cur["days"] = days()
            except ValueError as e:
                return {"ok": False, "message": str(e)}
            argv += ["--days", cur["days"]]
        if action == "lane-new" or "where" in f:
            argv.append("--local" if pick("where") == "local" else "--no-local")
            cur["local"] = pick("where") == "local"
        if action == "lane-new" or "note" in f:
            argv += ["--note", pick("note")]
        if action == "lane-new":
            if not pick("text"):
                return {"ok": False, "message": "A lane needs its text: what its house is to do."}
            if nm in load_lanes():
                return {"ok": False, "message": f"There's a loom lane {nm} already."}
            argv += ["-p", str(f.get("text") or "")]
        if len(argv) == 3:
            return {"ok": False, "message": "Nothing to change."}
        said = f"{pretty(nm)} is {name_of(cur.get('agent') or agent)}'s, {when_words(cur)}, {where_words(cur)}."
        if action == "lane-edit" and "note" in f and len(argv) == 5:
            said = f"{pretty(nm)}: what it's for is saved."
        return go(argv, said, page=f"lane/{nm}")
    if action == "lane-text":
        if not pick("text"):
            return {"ok": False, "message": "Paste the whole new text."}
        return go(["lane", "set", pick("name"), "-p", str(f.get("text") or "")], f"{pretty(pick('name'))}'s text is replaced.", page=f"lane/{pick('name')}")
    if action == "lane-rm":
        return go(["lane", "rm", pick("name")], f"Removed the loom lane {pretty(pick('name'))}.", page="")
    if action == "lane-run":
        ln = load_lanes().get(pick("name"))
        if not ln:
            return {"ok": False, "message": f"There's no loom lane {pick('name')}."}
        agent = ln["agent"]
        return go(["schedule", "run", pick("name"), "--note", "from loom"],
                  f"{pretty(pick('name'))} runs within a minute, {where_words(ln)}, as {name_of(agent)}.")
    if action == "lane-assign":
        to = pick("to")
        if not AGENT_NAME.match(to):
            return {"ok": False, "message": "Assign it to one of the household's agents."}
        return go(["lane", "assign", pick("name"), "--agent", to], f"{pretty(pick('name'))} is {name_of(to)}'s now.", page="")
    if action == "now":
        return go(["now"], f"{name} wakes within a minute.")
    if action == "clock":   # the clock's switch: on runs it, off pauses it
        action = "resume" if pick("on") == "on" else "pause"
    if action == "pause":
        return go(["pause"], f"{name}'s clock is paused. Wakes that come due are held.", undo={"action": "resume", "label": "Resume", "fields": {"agent": agent}})
    if action == "resume":
        return go(["resume"], f"{name}'s clock is running again.")
    if action == "run":
        return go(["schedule", "run", pick("name"), "--note", "from loom"], f"{pretty(pick('name'))} runs within a minute.")
    if action == "cancel":
        return go(["cancel", pick("id")], "Cancelled.", page="")
    if action == "schedule-rm":
        configure(agent)
        sc = load_schedules().get(pick("name"))
        configure(LOCAL_AGENT)
        if not sc:
            return {"ok": False, "message": "No such schedule."}
        runs = repo_relative(sc.get("prompt_file") or sc.get("lane") or "")
        undo = {"action": "schedule-set", "label": "Undo", "fields": {
            "agent": agent, "name": pick("name"), "at": sc["at"] if isinstance(sc["at"], str) else ",".join(sc["at"]),
            "days": sc.get("days", ""), "lane": runs, "note": sc.get("note", "")}}
        return go(["schedule", "rm", pick("name")], f"Removed {pretty(pick('name'))}.", page="", undo=undo)
    if action == "schedule-set":
        if agent == LOCAL_AGENT and lane_file(pick("lane")) is None:
            return {"ok": False, "message": f"Pick a lane: a file in {lane_dirs_text()}."}
        try:
            d = days()
        except ValueError as e:
            return {"ok": False, "message": str(e)}
        argv = ["schedule", "set", pick("name"), "--at", pick("at").replace(" ", ""), "-f", pick("lane")]
        if d:
            argv += ["--days", d]
        if pick("note"):
            argv += ["--note", pick("note")]
        if pick("model"):
            argv += ["--model", pick("model")]
        if pick("slot"):
            argv += ["--slot", pick("slot")]
        return go(argv, f"{pretty(pick('name'))} is scheduled: {when_text({'at': pick('at'), 'days': d})}.", page=f"schedule/{agent}/{pick('name')}")
    return {"ok": False, "message": "The clock doesn't know that action."}


def cmd_ui(args):
    if args.what is None:
        print(json.dumps(ui_manifest(ui_view())))
        return
    try:
        req = json.loads(sys.stdin.read() or "{}")
    except ValueError:
        req = {}
    own = owned_by(req.get("caller") if isinstance(req, dict) else None)
    if args.what == "page":
        path = req.get("path") if isinstance(req, dict) else ""
        view = [c for c in ui_view() if own is None or c["agent"] in own]
        if own is not None and str(path or "").startswith("lane/"):
            print(json.dumps({"title": "Not found", "sections": []}))
            return
        scope = os.environ.get("LOOM_SCOPE", "").strip()
        print(json.dumps(ui_page(view, path, lanes=own is None, scope=scope if AGENT_NAME.match(scope or "") else None)))
        return
    who = (req.get("caller") or {}).get("who") if isinstance(req, dict) and isinstance(req.get("caller"), dict) else None

    def run(agent, argv):
        # The page is the owner's: loom only runs a piece's ui for a signed-in owner.
        env = {**os.environ, "WAKE_ORIGIN": "", "WAKE_BY": (who if isinstance(who, str) and re.fullmatch(r"[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*", who) else None) or os.environ.get("LOOM_OWNER") or "the owner"}
        r = subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(SELF), "--agent", agent, *argv], capture_output=True, text=True,
                           cwd=REPO if REPO.is_dir() else HOME, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, timeout=12, env=env)
        return r.returncode, r.stdout, r.stderr
    print(json.dumps(ui_act(req, run)))


def forward(piece, argv):
    """Run this command as loom's piece instead, through loom's piece API (POST /api/<piece>/run) as this
    body's own token: LOOM_URL (the /mcp URL is fine) and LOOM_TOKEN_FILE (in a loom-box house,
    /run/secrets/loom-token by default). Prints what the piece printed and exits with its code."""
    url, tokfile = os.environ.get("LOOM_URL"), os.environ.get("LOOM_TOKEN_FILE")
    if not tokfile and os.path.exists("/run/secrets/loom-token"):
        tokfile = "/run/secrets/loom-token"
    if not url or not tokfile:
        sys.exit(f"{piece}: in a house this runs through loom's piece API: set LOOM_URL and LOOM_TOKEN_FILE")
    base = url.rstrip("/").removesuffix("/mcp")
    with open(tokfile) as f:
        token = f.read().strip()
    req = urllib.request.Request(f"{base}/api/{piece}/run", data=json.dumps({"argv": argv}).encode(), method="POST",
                                 headers={"content-type": "application/json", "authorization": f"Bearer {token}"})
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=60) as r:
            body = json.load(r)
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:
        try:
            why = json.load(e).get("error")
        except ValueError:
            why = None
        sys.exit(f"{piece}: loom refused {argv[0] if argv else 'the call'}: {why or f'{e.code} {e.reason}'}")
    except (urllib.error.URLError, OSError, ValueError) as e:
        sys.exit(f"{piece}: couldn't reach loom at {base}: {e}")
    sys.stdout.write(body.get("stdout") or "")
    sys.stderr.write(body.get("stderr") or "")
    code = body.get("exit")
    sys.exit(code if isinstance(code, int) else 1)


RUN_CHECK = 600   # seconds between the service's looks at the timers


def timer_active(wid):
    return subprocess.run(["systemctl", "--user", "is-active", "--quiet", unit_name(wid) + ".timer"],
                          capture_output=True).returncode == 0


def keep_armed():
    """Every clock's pending wakes have a timer: arm any that lost one (a reboot, a timer stopped by hand).
    A held wake (its clock is paused) waits for resume, not a timer."""
    for agent in clock_agents():
        configure(agent)
        with Spool() as spool:
            for e in spool.entries:
                if not e.get("held") and not timer_active(e["id"]):
                    if arm_timer(e) == "armed":
                        log("rearm", f"{e['id']} had no timer")
            ensure_deadman(spool)
    configure(LOCAL_AGENT)


def cmd_run(_args):
    """The piece's service: every clock's timers back at start (they're transient, so a reboot loses them),
    then kept armed. The wakes themselves run in their own transient units, not in this process.

    Until the owner names the local agent it arms nothing: loom starts a piece's services at install,
    before its settings are set, and a rearm then would plant a dead-man wake (a real session, a day
    later) for an agent nobody named. When the setting appears it exits, and systemd starts it afresh."""
    if not setting("WAKE_LOCAL_AGENT"):
        print("wake run: WAKE_LOCAL_AGENT isn't set (loom pieces set clock WAKE_LOCAL_AGENT=<agent>); "
              "arming nothing until it is", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
        while not (_owner_settings().get("WAKE_LOCAL_AGENT") or os.environ.get("WAKE_LOCAL_AGENT")):  # supervised: systemd stops it
            time.sleep(RUN_CHECK)
        sys.exit(1)   # configured now: Restart=on-failure starts it with the setting
    cmd_rearm(argparse.Namespace(every=True))
    sys.stdout.flush()
    last_armed = time.monotonic()
    while True:  # a supervised service: systemd stops it
        time.sleep(REAP_CHECK)
        try:
            configure(LOCAL_AGENT)
            reap_stuck()   # only the local agent's clock starts sessions here
        except (Exception, SystemExit) as e:   # a look that failed is tried again next time; never the service's end
            print(f"wake run: reap: {e}", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
        if time.monotonic() - last_armed < RUN_CHECK:
            continue
        last_armed = time.monotonic()
        try:
            keep_armed()
        except SystemExit as e:   # arm_timer's systemd-run failure: say it, keep going
            print(f"wake run: {e}", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)


def main():
    # In a house the clock isn't here: the spool is loom's machine's. A lane
    # that calls this script by its path, not the `wake` on PATH, would otherwise
    # write an alarm into the house's own copy, gone with the house. So every
    # command goes to the clock piece instead (WAKE_NO_FORWARD=1 keeps it here).
    if os.environ.get("HOUSE_ID") and not os.environ.get("WAKE_NO_FORWARD"):
        forward("clock", sys.argv[1:])
    # A `--principal <statement>` typed here (or left on by a wrapper) needs nothing on loom's machine, where a wake is
    # the owner's: taken off like the API door does. Over the API the statement comes in WAKE_PRINCIPAL_STATEMENT.
    sys.argv[1:], _ = split_principal(sys.argv[1:])
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="wake", description=__doc__, allow_abbrev=False,
                                 formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
    ap.add_argument("--agent", default=os.environ.get("WAKE_AGENT") or LOCAL_AGENT,
                    help=f"whose clock (default {LOCAL_AGENT}, WAKE_LOCAL_AGENT)")
    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest="cmd", required=True)

    def add_set(name, help_, parser_fn):
        p = sub.add_parser(name, help=help_, allow_abbrev=False)
        p.add_argument("time", nargs="+")
        p.add_argument("-p", "--prompt")
        p.add_argument("-f", "--prompt-file")
        p.add_argument("--note", default="")
        p.add_argument("--model", default=DEFAULT_MODEL)
        p.add_argument("--slot", default="", help="a house slot: its bookkeeping, restored and saved (one house at a time)")
        p.add_argument("--approval", default="", help="the owner's approval id, for a house's wake that must run on loom's machine")
        p.add_argument("--place", default="", help="the conversation it joins (delivery's place, like alert:host-watch): "
                       "every wake with the same place feeds one conversation; loom's machine only")
        p.set_defaults(fn=lambda a: cmd_set(a, parser_fn(a.time)))

    add_set("at", "wake at a clock time", parse_at)
    add_set("in", "wake after a duration", parse_in)
    p = sub.add_parser("park", help="blocked on the owner's answer (q-… or a-…): wake when they answer, then end", allow_abbrev=False)
    p.add_argument("--on", dest="park_on", required=True, help="the request's id: a secret's q-…, an approval's a-…")
    p.add_argument("-p", "--prompt", required=True, help="what to do next, told what they answered")
    p.add_argument("--note", default="")
    p.add_argument("--model", default=DEFAULT_MODEL)
    p.add_argument("--slot", default="")
    p.set_defaults(fn=cmd_park, prompt_file=None, approval="")
    sub.add_parser("list", help="show pending wakes").set_defaults(fn=cmd_list)
    p = sub.add_parser("log", help="the clock's record since a while ago", allow_abbrev=False)
    p.add_argument("--since", default="24h")
    p.add_argument("--grep", default="")
    p.set_defaults(fn=cmd_log)
    p = sub.add_parser("schedule", help="recurring wakes: set, rm, list", allow_abbrev=False)
    p.add_argument("action", choices=["set", "rm", "list", "run"])
    p.add_argument("name", nargs="?")
    p.add_argument("--at")
    p.add_argument("--days")
    p.add_argument("-p", "--prompt")
    p.add_argument("-f", "--prompt-file")
    p.add_argument("--note", default="")
    p.add_argument("--model", default=DEFAULT_MODEL)
    p.add_argument("--slot", default="", help="a house slot: its bookkeeping, restored and saved (one house at a time)")
    p.set_defaults(fn=cmd_schedule)
    p = sub.add_parser("lane", help="loom lanes: household work on a schedule, assigned to an agent", allow_abbrev=False)
    p.add_argument("action", choices=["set", "assign", "rm", "list", "text"])
    p.add_argument("name", nargs="?")
    p.add_argument("--agent", dest="lane_agent")
    p.add_argument("--at")
    p.add_argument("--days")
    p.add_argument("-p", "--prompt")
    p.add_argument("-f", "--prompt-file")
    p.add_argument("--note", default="")
    p.add_argument("--model", default="")
    p.add_argument("--local", action=argparse.BooleanOptionalAction, default=None, help="it needs loom's machine (systemd, files outside the repo); --no-local: a house")
    p.add_argument("--slot", default="", help="a house slot: the lane's bookkeeping between runs (one house at a time)")
    p.set_defaults(fn=cmd_lane)
    p = sub.add_parser("cancel", help="cancel a pending wake")
    p.add_argument("id")
    p.set_defaults(fn=cmd_cancel)
    sub.add_parser("rearm", help="recreate timers from spool (boot): every clock, unless --agent names one").set_defaults(fn=cmd_rearm)
    sub.add_parser("run", help="(service) rearm every clock, then keep every pending wake's timer armed").set_defaults(fn=cmd_run)
    sub.add_parser("reap", help="(service) stop this clock's sessions stuck on a permission prompt (WAKE_STUCK_AFTER)").set_defaults(fn=cmd_reap)
    p = sub.add_parser("bundle", help="(loom) this piece's part of the household bundle", allow_abbrev=False)
    p.add_argument("action", choices=["export", "import"])
    p.add_argument("--force", action="store_true")
    p.set_defaults(fn=cmd_bundle)
    sub.add_parser("pause", help="hold every wake that comes due").set_defaults(fn=cmd_pause)
    sub.add_parser("resume", help="unpause: held wakes fire once each").set_defaults(fn=cmd_resume)
    # Moved to loom's runtime; anything after the verb is taken and the answer says where it went.
    p = sub.add_parser("relay", help="(moved to loom's runtime: the relay tool, loom runtime relay)", allow_abbrev=False)
    p.set_defaults(fn=cmd_relay)
    p = sub.add_parser("relays", help="(moved to loom's runtime: loom runtime relays)", allow_abbrev=False)
    p.set_defaults(fn=cmd_relays)
    p = sub.add_parser("now", help="a wake within a minute, with no lane")
    p.add_argument("--note", default="")
    p.set_defaults(fn=cmd_now)
    p = sub.add_parser("fire", help="(internal) dispatch a wake")
    p.add_argument("id")
    p.set_defaults(fn=cmd_fire)
    p = sub.add_parser("ui", help="(loom) the page: manifest, or `ui page|act` with the request on stdin")
    p.add_argument("what", nargs="?", choices=["page", "act"])
    p.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    p.set_defaults(fn=cmd_ui)
    p = sub.add_parser("api", help="(loom) the piece API: request on stdin")
    p.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    p.set_defaults(fn=cmd_api)

    args, extra = ap.parse_known_args()
    # A relay's flags are the runtime's now: whatever came after `relay`, the answer says where it went.
    if extra and getattr(args, "fn", None) not in (cmd_relay, cmd_relays):
        ap.error(f"unrecognized arguments: {' '.join(extra)}")
    # A plain `wake rearm` (no --agent, as at boot) is every clock's.
    args.every = args.cmd == "rearm" and not any(a == "--agent" or a.startswith("--agent=") for a in sys.argv[1:]) \
        and not os.environ.get("WAKE_AGENT")
    if args.agent != AGENT:
        configure(args.agent)
    args.fn(args)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
